INSERT INTO _s463ep VALUES
(4291,'T','testaments-xii',18,6,'testaments-xii',18,6,$n$*And behold the heavens were opened, and an angel of Elohim (God) said to me, Levi, enter.* Levi, telling his sons of his vision (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 18:6), names the heavens-opening at the priestly investiture — the same heavens-opening Matt 3:16 narrates over Yahusha (Jesus) at the Yarden (Jordan). The Hebrew library knew the heavens open at the moment a covenant-bearing figure is invested for service; the gospel's opening of the heavens follows the same architecture.$n$,$n$And behold the heavens were opened, and an angel of Elohim (God) said to me, Levi, enter.$n$,false),
(4339,'T','testaments-xii',100,2,'testaments-xii',100,2,$n$*But I say unto you, That whosoever is angry with his brother without a cause shall be in danger of the judgment: and whosoever shall say to his brother, Raca, shall be in danger of the council: but whosoever shall say, Thou fool, shall be in danger of hell fire.* (Matthew 5:22). *For in the presence of my father I spake peaceably to Joseph; and when I had gone out, the spirit of hatred darkened my mind, and stirred up my soul to slay him.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 100:2). Gad is speaking to his sons about what he did to Joseph. In front of their father he spoke peaceably, and the moment he had gone out hatred darkened his mind and drove his soul toward killing his brother. That is the road Yahusha (Jesus) is describing: the commandment against murder was never only about the hand, because anger at a brother is where the killing begins. He is not setting the Torah aside but reading the commandment down to its root, the same root Gad learned the hard way and warned his children about.$n$,$n$For in the presence of my father I spake peaceably to Joseph; and when I had gone out, the spirit of hatred darkened my mind, and stirred up my soul to slay him.$n$,true),
(4341,'T','testaments-xii',100,3,'testaments-xii',100,3,$n$*But I say unto you, Love your enemies, bless them that curse you, do good to them that hate you, and pray for them which despitefully use you, and persecute you;* (Matthew 5:44). *Love ye one another from the heart; and if a man sin against thee, speak peaceably to him, and in thy soul hold not guile; and if he repent and confess, forgive him.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 100:3). Gad does not stop at loving the brother who treats you well. If a man sins against you, speak peaceably to him, keep no guile in your soul, and forgive him when he repents. Yahusha (Jesus) reaches the same place from the other side, telling us to bless those who curse us, do good to those who hate us, and pray for those who persecute us. This is not a teaching set against Moses; the fathers were already handing it to their sons, and Gad hands it down out of what hatred did to Joseph.$n$,$n$Love ye one another from the heart; and if a man sin against thee, speak peaceably to him, and in thy soul hold not guile; and if he repent and confess, forgive him.$n$,true),
(4427,'T','2-baruch',70,2,'2-baruch',70,2,$n$*Then saith he unto his disciples, The harvest truly is plenteous, but the labourers are few;* (Matthew 9:37). *Behold! the days come, and it shall be when the time of the age has ripened, And the harvest of its evil and good seeds has come, That the Mighty One will bring upon the earth and its inhabitants and upon its rulers Perturbation of spirit and stupor of heart.* (2 Baruch 70:2). Baruch looks ahead to the time when the age has ripened and the harvest of its evil and good seeds has come, and the Mighty One brings bewilderment on the earth and its rulers. Yahusha (Jesus), looking at the crowds, says the harvest truly is plenteous, and the labourers are few. What Baruch placed at the end of the age, Yahusha (Jesus) says is already at hand. Both speak of a harvest of two kinds of seed, which is why the sorting matters and why labourers are wanted.$n$,$n$Behold! the days come, and it shall be when the time of the age has ripened, And the harvest of its evil and good seeds has come, That the Mighty One will bring upon the earth and its inhabitants and upon its rulers Perturbation of spirit and stupor of heart.$n$,true),
(4428,'T','2-baruch',70,2,'2-baruch',70,2,$n$*Pray ye therefore Yahuah (Lord) of the harvest, that he will send forth labourers into his harvest.* (Matthew 9:38) *Behold! the days come, and it shall be when the time of the age has ripened, And the harvest of its evil and good seeds has come, That the Mighty One will bring upon the earth and its inhabitants and upon its rulers Perturbation of spirit and stupor of heart.* (2 Baruch 70:2) Yahusha (Jesus) sees the crowds and tells his disciples to ask Yahuah (Lord) of the harvest for labourers, because the harvest is standing ready. Baruch had already been told what that harvest is: the time of the age ripens, and what was sown in it, evil seed and good seed alike, has come up. The one Baruch calls the Mighty One is the owner of that field, so the prayer in Matthew is a prayer prayed inside that ripening time, and the next chapter sends the twelve out as the answer.$n$,$n$Behold! the days come, and it shall be when the time of the age has ripened, And the harvest of its evil and good seeds has come, That the Mighty One will bring upon the earth and its inhabitants and upon its rulers Perturbation of spirit and stupor of heart.$n$,true),
(4431,'T','2-baruch',78,3,'2-baruch',78,3,$n$*But when he saw the multitudes, he was moved with compassion on them, because they fainted, and were scattered abroad, as sheep having no shepherd.* (Matthew 9:36) *And truly I know that behold all we the twelve tribes are bound by one bond, inasmuch as we are born from one father.* (2 Baruch 78:3) Yahusha (Jesus) looks at the multitudes and finds them scattered and without a shepherd, which is a picture of a people and not of a crowd of strangers. Baruch writes to the brethren in captivity and says who that people is: the twelve tribes, bound by one bond because they are born from one father. However far they have been carried, they are one flock by birth, and that is what moves Yahusha (Jesus) to compassion.$n$,$n$And truly I know that behold all we the twelve tribes are bound by one bond, inasmuch as we are born from one father.$n$,true),
(4432,'T','2-baruch',78,7,'2-baruch',78,7,$n$*But when he saw the multitudes, he was moved with compassion on them, because they fainted, and were scattered abroad, as sheep having no shepherd.* (Matthew 9:36) *For if ye so do these things, He will continually remember you, He who always promised on our behalf to those who were more excellent than we, that He will never forget or forsake us, but with much mercy will gather together again those who were dispersed.* (2 Baruch 78:7) Yahusha (Jesus) is moved with compassion at sheep scattered abroad with no shepherd. Baruch closes his letter to the scattered tribes with the promise that answers it: Yahuah (Lord) will never forget or forsake them, and with much mercy will gather together again those who were dispersed. The compassion in Matthew and the mercy in Baruch are one mercy, and its work is the gathering.$n$,$n$For if ye so do these things, He will continually remember you, He who always promised on our behalf to those who were more excellent than we, that He will never forget or forsake us, but with much mercy will gather together again those who were dispersed.$n$,true),
(4695,'T','testaments-xii',100,3,'testaments-xii',100,3,$n$*So likewise shall my heavenly Father do also unto you, if ye from your hearts forgive not every one his brother their trespasses.* (Matthew 18:35). *Love ye one another from the heart; and if a man sin against thee, speak peaceably to him, and in thy soul hold not guile; and if he repent and confess, forgive him.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 100:3). Yahusha (Jesus) closes His warning with the words from your hearts: the Father will deal with us as we deal with a brother we will not forgive. Gad gives his sons the same measure. Love one another from the heart, speak peaceably to a brother who sins against you, and when he repents and confesses, forgive him. Both put the whole matter in the heart, where a brother is either forgiven or kept in the ledger.$n$,$n$Love ye one another from the heart; and if a man sin against thee, speak peaceably to him, and in thy soul hold not guile; and if he repent and confess, forgive him.$n$,true),
(4710,'T','testaments-xii',29,5,'testaments-xii',29,5,$n$*Yahusha (Jesus) said unto him, If thou wilt be perfect, go and sell that thou hast, and give to the poor, and thou shalt have treasure in heaven: and come and follow me.* (Matthew 19:21) *Work righteousness, therefore, my children, upon the earth, That ye may have (it) as a treasure in heaven.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 29:5) Yahusha (Jesus) tells the rich young man that if he wants to be perfect he should go, sell what he has, give to the poor, and have treasure in heaven, and then come and follow. Levi tells his sons the same thing in other words: work righteousness on the earth, and it is kept as a treasure in heaven. Just before this, Yahusha (Jesus) had told the man that the way into life is to keep the commandments, so the treasure in heaven is what righteousness done on the earth is laid up as.$n$,$n$Work righteousness, therefore, my children, upon the earth, That ye may have (it) as a treasure in heaven.$n$,true),
(4720,'T','testaments-xii',129,2,'testaments-xii',129,2,$n$*And Yahusha (Jesus) said unto them, Verily I say unto you, That ye which have followed me, in the regeneration when the Son of Adam shall sit in the throne of his glory, ye also shall sit upon twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Yashar'el (Israel).* (Matthew 19:28). *There were twelve harts feeding: and the nine were (first) dispersed over all the earth, and likewise also the three.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 129:2). Joseph sees twelve harts feeding together, and all twelve end up dispersed over the earth, the nine first and the three likewise. The twelve harts read as the twelve tribes, scattered. Yahusha (Jesus) speaks of those same tribes as a whole people sitting under judgment when the Son of Adam takes His throne, with twelve thrones set for judging the twelve tribes of Yashar'el (Israel). A people who are to be judged as twelve tribes must first be gathered as twelve, and Joseph's vision is the scattering that the gathering answers.$n$,$n$There were twelve harts feeding: and the nine were (first) dispersed over all the earth, and likewise also the three.$n$,true),
(4737,'T','testaments-xii',139,5,'testaments-xii',139,5,$n$*Even as the Son of Adam came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many.* (Matthew 20:28). *And He shall ascend from Hades and shall pass from earth into heaven. And I know how lowly He shall be upon earth, and how glorious in heaven.]* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 139:5). Yahusha (Jesus) says of Himself that the Son of Adam came not to be served but to serve, and to give His life a ransom for many. Benjamin, looking ahead, says he knows how lowly He will be upon the earth and how glorious in heaven. The lowliness and the glory belong to one person: the one who takes the servant's place on earth is the one who ascends from Hades into heaven.$n$,$n$And He shall ascend from Hades and shall pass from earth into heaven. And I know how lowly He shall be upon earth, and how glorious in heaven.]$n$,true),
(4739,'T','testaments-xii',58,5,'testaments-xii',59,1,$n$*And, behold, two blind men sitting by the way side, when they heard that Yahusha (Jesus) passed by, cried out, saying, Have mercy on us, O Adonai (Lord), thou Son of David.* (Matthew 20:30). *And after these things shall a star arise to you from Jacob in peace, And a man shall arise [from my seed], like the sun of righteousness, Walking with the sons of men in meekness and righteousness; And no sin shall be found in him.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 59:1). Yahudah (Judah) tells his sons that a star will rise to them out of Jacob, a man from his own seed who walks among the sons of men in meekness and without sin. Two blind men by the Jericho road, who cannot see him, cry out to him by that very title, Son of David, the seed of Yahudah (Judah). The testament named the man; the blind men recognized him by his line before they could see his face.$n$,$n$And after these things shall a star arise to you from Jacob in peace, And a man shall arise [from my seed], like the sun of righteousness, Walking with the sons of men in meekness and righteousness; And no sin shall be found in him.$n$,true),
(4740,'T','testaments-xii',59,4,'testaments-xii',59,4,$n$*And, behold, two blind men sitting by the way side, when they heard that Yahusha (Jesus) passed by, cried out, saying, Have mercy on us, O Adonai (Lord), thou Son of David.* (Matthew 20:30) *[This Branch of Elohim (God) El Elyon (Most High), And this Fountain giving life unto all.]* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 59:4) The two blind men call Yahusha (Jesus) the Son of David. The verse before this one has Yahudah (Judah) saying his sons will be sons in truth and will walk in His commandments first and last, and then he names the Branch of Elohim (God) that comes from his line and the Fountain giving life to all. The Son of David the blind men name is that Branch, and men who cannot see are the ones who know him by hearing his voice as he passes.$n$,$n$[This Branch of Elohim (God) El Elyon (Most High), And this Fountain giving life unto all.]$n$,true),
(4741,'T','testaments-xii',59,5,'testaments-xii',59,5,$n$*And the multitude rebuked them, because they should hold their peace: but they cried the more, saying, Have mercy on us, O Adonai (Lord), thou Son of David.* (Matthew 20:31) *Then shall the sceptre of my kingdom shine forth; And from your root shall arise a stem;* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 59:5) The multitude tells the blind men to hold their peace, and they cry out all the more, Son of David. Yahudah (Judah) says the sceptre of his kingdom will shine forth and a stem will rise from the root of his sons. The two men have no sight, yet they name the stem from the root of Yahudah (Judah) while the crowd, which can see, tries to silence them. They show what Yahusha (Jesus) said of his own sheep, that they hear his voice.$n$,$n$Then shall the sceptre of my kingdom shine forth; And from your root shall arise a stem;$n$,true),
(4742,'T','testaments-xii',59,5,'testaments-xii',59,5,$n$*Tell ye the daughter of Sion, Behold, thy King cometh unto thee, meek, and sitting upon an ass, and a colt the foal of an ass.* (Matthew 21:5) *Then shall the sceptre of my kingdom shine forth; And from your root shall arise a stem;* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 59:5) Matthew shows the King coming to the daughter of Zion, meek and sitting on an ass, as the prophet had said. Yahudah (Judah) told his sons that the sceptre of his kingdom would shine forth and a stem rise from their root. The sceptre promised to the tribe of Yahudah (Judah) arrives not in a chariot but on a colt, and the daughter of Zion is told to look.$n$,$n$Then shall the sceptre of my kingdom shine forth; And from your root shall arise a stem;$n$,true),
(4743,'T','testaments-xii',59,6,'testaments-xii',59,6,$n$*Tell ye the daughter of Sion, Behold, thy King cometh unto thee, meek, and sitting upon an ass, and a colt the foal of an ass.* (Matthew 21:5) *And from it shall grow a rod of righteousness to the Gentiles, To judge and to save all that call upon Yahuah (Lord).* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 59:6) Matthew shows the King coming to the daughter of Zion, meek, on a colt. Yahudah (Judah) says a rod of righteousness will grow from the stem that comes from his root, to judge and to save all who call upon Yahuah (Lord). The Gentiles here are best read as the scattered seed of Yashar'el (Israel) living among the nations, the ones the King is coming to gather and who call out to him, as the crowds of the entry will do. This is not a new people set in the place of the twelve tribes.$n$,$n$And from it shall grow a rod of righteousness to the Gentiles, To judge and to save all that call upon Yahuah (Lord).$n$,true),
(4789,'T','testaments-xii',26,3,'testaments-xii',26,3,$n$*But woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye shut up the kingdom of heaven against men: for ye neither go in yourselves, neither suffer ye them that are entering to go in.* (Matthew 23:13) *And ye shall deal lawlessly together with Yashar'el (Israel), so He shall not bear with Jerusalem because of your wickedness; but the veil of the temple shall be rent, so as not to cover your shame.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 26:3) Yahusha (Jesus) charges the scribes and Pharisees with shutting up the kingdom of heaven against men, going in neither themselves nor letting others enter. Levi foresaw leaders of his own line dealing lawlessly with Yashar'el (Israel), and the veil of the temple being rent so that it would no longer cover their shame. In both the failing is a leadership that holds the door and breaks the commandments, and the people kept out are its victims. When the veil of the temple is torn at his death, the lawlessness of the keepers is laid bare.$n$,$n$And ye shall deal lawlessly together with Yashar'el (Israel), so He shall not bear with Jerusalem because of your wickedness; but the veil of the temple shall be rent, so as not to cover your shame.$n$,true),
(4790,'T','testaments-xii',33,11,'testaments-xii',33,11,$n$*Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye compass sea and land to make one proselyte, and when he is made, ye make him twofold more the child of hell than yourselves.* (Matthew 23:15) *And in the seventh week shall come priests, (who are) idolaters, adulterers, lovers of money, proud, lawless, lascivious, abusers of children and beasts.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 33:11) Yahusha (Jesus) says the scribes and Pharisees cross sea and land to make one proselyte, and when he is made they make him twofold more the child of hell than themselves. Levi's vision of the weeks names the priests who come in the seventh week as idolaters, lovers of money, proud and lawless. A convert made by leaders like that is made into what they are, which is why the measure is whether a teacher keeps the commandments. The fault is in the system that made the proselyte, and the one it made is its victim.$n$,$n$And in the seventh week shall come priests, (who are) idolaters, adulterers, lovers of money, proud, lawless, lascivious, abusers of children and beasts.$n$,true),
(4798,'T','testaments-xii',105,1,'testaments-xii',105,1,$n$*Even so ye also outwardly appear righteous unto men, but within ye are full of hypocrisy and iniquity.* (Matthew 23:28). *But do not ye, my children, wear two faces like unto them, of goodness and of wickedness; but cleave unto goodness only, for Elohim (God) hath His habitation therein, and men desire it.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 105:1). Yahusha (Jesus) names the double face plainly: outwardly righteous before men, inwardly full of hypocrisy and iniquity. Asher warns his sons against exactly that, to wear one face and not two, and to cleave to goodness only because Elohim (God) makes His habitation there. What Yahusha (Jesus) exposes in the hypocrite, Asher tells his children to refuse before it ever takes root.$n$,$n$But do not ye, my children, wear two faces like unto them, of goodness and of wickedness; but cleave unto goodness only, for Elohim (God) hath His habitation therein, and men desire it.$n$,true),
(4799,'T','testaments-xii',108,2,'testaments-xii',108,2,$n$*Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye are like unto whited sepulchres, which indeed appear beautiful outward, but are within full of dead men’s bones, and of all uncleanness.* (Matthew 23:27). *For they that are double-faced are guilty of a twofold sin; 'for they both do the evil thing and they have pleasure in them that do it', following the example of the spirits of deceit, and striving against mankind.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 108:2). Yahusha (Jesus) calls the hypocrites whited sepulchres, beautiful on the outside and full of death within. Asher gives the same condition its weight: the double-faced are guilty of a twofold sin, because they do the evil thing and also take pleasure in those who do it. The tomb is the picture of the sin Asher counts twice, a clean outside covering what is in fact within.$n$,$n$For they that are double-faced are guilty of a twofold sin; 'for they both do the evil thing and they have pleasure in them that do it', following the example of the spirits of deceit, and striving against mankind.$n$,true),
(4824,'T','testaments-xii',90,1,'testaments-xii',90,1,$n$*And as he sat upon the mount of Olives, the disciples came unto him privately, saying, Tell us, when shall these things be? and what shall be the sign of thy coming, and of the end of the world?* (Matthew 24:3) *For in the fortieth year of my life, I saw a vision on the Mount of Olives, on the east of Jerusalem, that the sun and the moon were standing still.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 90:1) The disciples sit on the mount of Olives and ask Yahusha (Jesus) the sign of his coming and of the end of the world. Naphtali, in the fortieth year of his life, saw a vision on that same mountain, east of Jerusalem. It is a place where what is coming is shown and asked about, and the two come together there.$n$,$n$For in the fortieth year of my life, I saw a vision on the Mount of Olives, on the east of Jerusalem, that the sun and the moon were standing still.$n$,true),
(4825,'T','testaments-xii',93,3,'testaments-xii',93,3,$n$*And this gospel of the kingdom shall be preached in all the world for a witness unto all nations; and then shall the end come.* (Matthew 24:14) *For through their tribes shall Elohim (God) appear [dwelling among men] on earth, To save the race of Yashar'el (Israel), And to gather together the righteous from amongst the Gentiles.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 93:3) Yahusha (Jesus) says the gospel of the kingdom will be preached in all the world as a witness to all nations, and then the end comes. Naphtali's last words say what the news is: Elohim (God) appears through the tribes to save the race of Yashar'el (Israel) and to gather the righteous from among the Gentiles. The Gentiles here are best read as the scattered seed of the twelve tribes living among the nations, which is why the news goes out broadly: the sheep are scattered everywhere, are not known by sight, and hear when they are called.$n$,$n$For through their tribes shall Elohim (God) appear [dwelling among men] on earth, To save the race of Yashar'el (Israel), And to gather together the righteous from amongst the Gentiles.$n$,true),
(4826,'T','testaments-xii',109,2,'testaments-xii',109,3,$n$*And then shall appear the sign of the Son of Adam in heaven: and then shall all the tribes of the earth mourn, and they shall see the Son of Adam coming in the clouds of heaven with power and great glory.* (Matthew 24:30). *Until the El Elyon (Most High) shall visit the earth, coming Himself [as man, with men eating and drinking], and breaking the head of the dragon in the water. He shall save Yashar'el (Israel) and all the Gentiles [Elohim (God) speaking in the person of man].* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 109:3). Asher has just told his sons that they will sin, be handed to their enemies, and be scattered to the four corners of the earth. Then he says the Most High will visit the earth, coming Himself as man, and will save Yashar'el (Israel) and the Gentiles, who stand right beside the scattered of the verse before. Matthew shows the same one at the end of that road, the sign of the Son of Adam in heaven, all the tribes of the earth mourning, and the Son of Adam coming in the clouds with power and great glory. The one who comes in the person of man is Yahusha (Jesus), the one in whom Elohim (God) took form, who walked with Adam's line from the beginning and came in flesh, and the tribes that mourn are the tribes Asher says were scattered.$n$,$n$Until the El Elyon (Most High) shall visit the earth, coming Himself [as man, with men eating and drinking], and breaking the head of the dragon in the water. He shall save Yashar'el (Israel) and all the Gentiles [Elohim (God) speaking in the person of man].$n$,true),
(4827,'T','testaments-xii',109,7,'testaments-xii',109,7,$n$*And he shall send his angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from one end of heaven to the other.* (Matthew 24:31). *But Yahuah (Lord) will gather you together in faith through His tender mercy, 'and' for the sake of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.]* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 109:7). The sons of Asher are told they will be scattered until they do not know their own lands, tribe, and tongue. Yet Yahuah (the Lord) will gather them, and the reason given is Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob: the gathering rests on the fathers and on the blood that carries their promise. Matthew has the same gathering in view, with the elect called in from the four winds. The elect there are the scattered seed of the fathers being brought home, and not a company assembled out of any people by confession.$n$,$n$But Yahuah (Lord) will gather you together in faith through His tender mercy, 'and' for the sake of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.]$n$,true),
(4861,'T','testaments-xii',26,2,'testaments-xii',26,2,$n$*Then saith Yahusha (Jesus) unto them, All ye shall be offended because of me this night: for it is written, I will smite the shepherd, and the sheep of the flock shall be scattered abroad.* (Matthew 26:31) *And behold, I am clear from your ungodliness and transgression, which ye shall commit in the end of the ages [against the Saviour of the world, Messiah (Christ), acting godlessly], deceiving Yashar'el (Israel), and stirring up against it great evils from Yahuah (Lord).* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 26:2) On the night of his arrest Yahusha (Jesus) tells his disciples they will all be offended because of him, and says it is written that the shepherd will be smitten and the sheep scattered. Long before, Levi told his sons that at the end of the ages they would act ungodly against the Saviour of the world, deceiving Yashar'el (Israel) and leaving it open to great evils. Both describe leadership failing and the flock scattered as a result. The one who is smitten was himself born of Yahudah (Judah) and came for his people, so what is named here is a corrupt leadership, not the people.$n$,$n$And behold, I am clear from your ungodliness and transgression, which ye shall commit in the end of the ages [against the Saviour of the world, Messiah (Christ), acting godlessly], deceiving Yashar'el (Israel), and stirring up against it great evils from Yahuah (Lord).$n$,true),
(4862,'T','testaments-xii',26,3,'testaments-xii',26,3,$n$*Then the high priest rent his clothes, saying, He hath spoken blasphemy; what further need have we of witnesses? behold, now ye have heard his blasphemy.* (Matthew 26:65) *And ye shall deal lawlessly together with Yashar'el (Israel), so He shall not bear with Jerusalem because of your wickedness; but the veil of the temple shall be rent, so as not to cover your shame.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 26:3) The high priest tears his own clothes and calls the truth blasphemy, though the Torah forbids the high priest to rend his clothes. Levi had said that when the lawlessness of the leaders of his line was full, it would be the veil of the temple that was rent, so as not to cover their shame. One rending is a man's, done in anger to silence a witness; the other is Yahuah's (God's), and it uncovers. The charge is against the office as it was being used, not against the people under it.$n$,$n$And ye shall deal lawlessly together with Yashar'el (Israel), so He shall not bear with Jerusalem because of your wickedness; but the veil of the temple shall be rent, so as not to cover your shame.$n$,true),
(4863,'T','testaments-xii',133,6,'testaments-xii',133,8,$n$*For this is my blood of the new testament, which is shed for many for the remission of sins.* (Matthew 26:28). *In thee shall be fulfilled the prophecy of heaven [concerning the Lamb of Elohim (God), and Saviour of the world], that a blameless one shall be delivered up for lawless men, and a sinless shall die for ungodly men [in the blood of the covenant, for the salvation of the Gentiles and 'of Israel', and shall destroy Beliar and his servants].* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 133:8). Jacob, embracing Joseph, tells him that in him the prophecy of heaven will be fulfilled: a blameless one delivered up for lawless men, a sinless one dying for ungodly men in the blood of the covenant. Yahusha (Jesus) at the table gives that blood its name, shed for many for the remission of sins. The Testament says the salvation is for the Gentiles and for the house of Yashar'el (Israel), and the Gentiles named beside Yashar'el (Israel) are the scattered seed of the house of Yashar'el (Israel) living among the nations, which is why the news goes out broadly: the sheep are scattered everywhere, and the ones who hear are the ones it was always for.$n$,$n$In thee shall be fulfilled the prophecy of heaven [concerning the Lamb of Elohim (God), and Saviour of the world], that a blameless one shall be delivered up for lawless men, and a sinless shall die for ungodly men [in the blood of the covenant, for the salvation of the Gentiles and 'of Israel', and shall destroy Beliar and his servants].$n$,true),
(4869,'T','2-baruch',6,7,'2-baruch',6,7,$n$*And, behold, the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom; and the earth did quake, and the rocks rent;* (Matthew 27:51). *And I saw him descend into the Holy of Holies, and take from thence the veil, and the holy ark, and the mercy-seat, and the two tables, and the holy raiment of the priests, and the altar of incense, and the forty-eight precious stones, wherewith the priest was adorned and all the holy vessels of the tabernacle.* (2 Baruch 6:7). The veil is torn from the top to the bottom, which is a tearing from above. In 2 Baruch the hand from above also acts upon the veil: the angel descends into the Holy of Holies and takes from there the veil, the ark, the mercy seat and every holy vessel, and the next verse in the book says he charges the earth to guard them until the last times so that strangers may not get possession of them. In neither is the house of Yahuah (God) simply done away with. In Baruch its holy things are kept to be restored, and in Matthew the veil is opened from above, and the way back into the holiest is the way home.$n$,$n$And I saw him descend into the Holy of Holies, and take from thence the veil, and the holy ark, and the mercy-seat, and the two tables, and the holy raiment of the priests, and the altar of incense, and the forty-eight precious stones, wherewith the priest was adorned and all the holy vessels of the tabernacle.$n$,true),
(4870,'T','testaments-xii',20,5,'testaments-xii',21,1,$n$*And, behold, the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom; and the earth did quake, and the rocks rent;* (Matthew 27:51). *And thereupon the angel opened to me the gates of heaven, and I saw the holy temple, and upon a throne of glory the El Elyon (Most High).* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 21:1). Levi is shown the gates of heaven opened and the holy temple with the throne of glory inside it. At the death of Yahusha (Jesus) the veil that closed the earthly holy of holies is torn from the top down, opened from heaven's side and not from ours. What Levi saw opened in vision is opened in fact at the cross, and the way into the holiest is laid bare.$n$,$n$And thereupon the angel opened to me the gates of heaven, and I saw the holy temple, and upon a throne of glory the El Elyon (Most High).$n$,true),
(4871,'T','testaments-xii',21,2,'testaments-xii',21,2,$n$*And, behold, the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom; and the earth did quake, and the rocks rent;* (Matthew 27:51) *And He said to me: Levi, I have given thee the blessings of the priesthood until I come and sojourn in the midst of Yashar'el (Israel).* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 21:2) Levi is told that the blessings of the priesthood are his until Yahuah (Lord) comes and sojourns in the midst of Yashar'el (Israel). Matthew shows what the end of that until looks like: when Yahusha (Jesus) has come and given his life, the veil of the temple is torn from the top to the bottom, and the way into the holy place stands open. Nothing of Torah is thrown out in this; the way to the Father is opened from above by the one who came to sojourn among his people.$n$,$n$And He said to me: Levi, I have given thee the blessings of the priesthood until I come and sojourn in the midst of Yashar'el (Israel).$n$,true),
(4872,'T','testaments-xii',24,17,'testaments-xii',24,17,$n$*And the graves were opened; and many bodies of the saints which slept arose,* (Matthew 27:52) *And some of them shall be high priests, and judges, and scribes; For by their mouth shall the holy place be guarded.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 24:17) Levi is told that some of his seed will be high priests, judges and scribes, and that the holy place will be guarded by what they say. Matthew shows the saints who slept rising out of opened graves when Yahusha (Jesus) dies, which can be read as a foretaste of the resurrection of the faithful that is still ahead. The two meet on the same ground: the holy place and the faithful who served Yahuah (God) in it are not left to the grave.$n$,$n$And some of them shall be high priests, and judges, and scribes; For by their mouth shall the holy place be guarded.$n$,true),
(4884,'T','2-baruch',51,7,'2-baruch',51,7,$n$*And the graves were opened; and many bodies of the saints which slept arose,* (Matthew 27:52). *But those who have been saved by their works, And to whom the law has been now a hope, And understanding an expectation, And wisdom a confidence, Shall wonders appear in their time. For they shall behold the world which is now invisible to them, And they shall behold the time which is now hidden from them:* (2 Baruch 51:7–8). Matthew says the graves were opened and many bodies of the saints which slept arose. Baruch speaks of people for whom the law was a hope, an understanding and a confidence, and says wonders will appear in their time and they will behold the world that is now invisible to them. These are people whose whole life was the Torah, and nothing here sets their works against the promise. It describes the covenant walk of those who kept the commandments, and the opened graves at the cross are the first glimpse of the seeing that is promised to them.$n$,$n$But those who have been saved by their works, And to whom the law has been now a hope, And understanding an expectation, And wisdom a confidence, Shall wonders appear in their time.$n$,true),
(4908,'T','testaments-xii',139,5,'testaments-xii',139,5,$n$*And Yahusha (Jesus) came and spake unto them, saying, All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth.* (Matthew 28:18). *And He shall ascend from Hades and shall pass from earth into heaven. And I know how lowly He shall be upon earth, and how glorious in heaven.]* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 139:5). Benjamin says the one who comes will ascend from Hades and pass from earth into heaven, lowly on the earth and glorious in heaven. After the cross and the tomb, Yahusha (Jesus) comes to His disciples and says all power is given to Him in heaven and in earth. The word Benjamin gave his sons is the road that ends in that sentence.$n$,$n$And He shall ascend from Hades and shall pass from earth into heaven. And I know how lowly He shall be upon earth, and how glorious in heaven.]$n$,true),
(4909,'T','testaments-xii',140,5,'testaments-xii',140,5,$n$*Go ye therefore, and teach all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit):* (Matthew 28:19). *For all these things they gave us for an inheritance, saying: Keep the commandments of Elohim (God), until Yahuah (Lord) shall reveal His salvation to all Gentiles.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 140:5). The fathers left their sons the commandments of Elohim (God) as their inheritance, to be kept while they waited for Yahuah (the Lord) to reveal His salvation to all the Gentiles. The until marks the length of the waiting, not an end to the keeping. When Yahusha (Jesus) says to go and teach all nations, the message goes out broadly because those it is for are scattered among them and are not known by sight. Benjamin's word has the order right: the commandments stay in the hands of the sons, and the salvation goes out to be heard.$n$,$n$For all these things they gave us for an inheritance, saying: Keep the commandments of Elohim (God), until Yahuah (Lord) shall reveal His salvation to all Gentiles.$n$,true),
(4910,'T','testaments-xii',140,7,'testaments-xii',140,7,$n$*Then said Yahusha (Jesus) unto them, Be not afraid: go tell my brethren that they go into Galilee, and there shall they see me.* (Matthew 28:10). *Then shall we also rise, each one over our tribe, worshipping the King of heaven, [who appeared upon earth in the form of a man in humility. And as many as believe on Him on the earth shall rejoice with Him].* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 140:7). After His resurrection Yahusha (Jesus) tells the women to carry word to His brethren, and the brethren He means are sons of Yashar'el (Israel). Benjamin pictures that same people rising from the dead, each patriarch over his own tribe, worshipping the King of heaven who appeared on earth in the form of a man. The Testament keeps the tribes by name and by order, and the Messiah (Christ) still calls them brethren.$n$,$n$Then shall we also rise, each one over our tribe, worshipping the King of heaven, [who appeared upon earth in the form of a man in humility. And as many as believe on Him on the earth shall rejoice with Him].$n$,true),
(4911,'T','testaments-xii',140,8,'testaments-xii',140,8,$n$*And Yahusha (Jesus) came and spake unto them, saying, All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth.* (Matthew 28:18). *Then also all men shall rise, some unto glory and some unto shame. And Yahuah (Lord) shall judge Yashar'el (Israel) first, for their unrighteousness; [for when He appeared as Elohim (God) in the flesh to deliver them they believed Him not].* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 140:8). Benjamin says all men shall rise, some to glory and some to shame, and that Yahuah (the Lord) will judge Yashar'el (Israel) first because they did not believe Him when He appeared as Elohim (God) in the flesh. Yahusha (Jesus) says all power is given to Him in heaven and in earth, and a judge needs that power. Judgment beginning with the house of the fathers is the order the Testament lays out, and Yahusha (Jesus) is the one who holds the authority to carry it through.$n$,$n$Then also all men shall rise, some unto glory and some unto shame. And Yahuah (Lord) shall judge Yashar'el (Israel) first, for their unrighteousness; [for when He appeared as Elohim (God) in the flesh to deliver them they believed Him not].$n$,true),
(8023,'T','testaments-xii',134,5,'testaments-xii',134,5,$n$*Greater love hath no man than this, that a man lay down his life for his friends.* (John 15:13). *And him that hath the grace of a good spirit he loveth as his own soul.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 134:5). Yahusha (Jesus) names the greatest love as laying down one's life for his friends. Benjamin teaches his sons the same love at its starting measure: the man with the grace of a good spirit loves his brother as his own soul. A man who loves another as his own soul has already begun to hold his own life loosely, and the Messiah (Christ) carries that love to its furthest end.$n$,$n$And him that hath the grace of a good spirit he loveth as his own soul.$n$,true),
(8025,'T','testaments-xii',100,2,'testaments-xii',100,1,$n$*love one another in deed, and in word, and in the inclination of the soul.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 100:1). Gad carries the love-one-another command in his own testimony to his sons, and he names it out of his own repentance for the hatred he bore against Joseph his brother. Yahusha's (Jesus') *a new commandment I give unto you, That ye love one another* (John 13:34) is *new* not because the Hebrew library never named brotherly love, but because he loves *as I have loved you* — the patriarch's heart-command brought to its measure in the Formed one's own laying-down of his life. The wisdom of the fathers already pressed the command on the twelve sons of Yashar'el (Israel); the gospel binds it to the cross.$n$,$n$And now, my children, 'I exhort you,' love ye each one his brother, and put away hatred from your hearts, love one another in deed, and in word, and in the inclination of the soul.$n$,false),
(51071,'S','3-baruch',12,5,'3-baruch',12,5,$n$Revelation 14:13 — *Blessed are the dead which die in Yahusha (Lord) from henceforth: Yea, saith the Spirit, that they may rest from their labours; and their works do follow them.* The flowers that are the merits of the righteous, carried up to God, are the works John says follow the saints who die in the Lord.$n$,$n$And the angel said to me, These flowers are the merits of the righteous.$n$,false),
(51087,'S','3-baruch',15,2,'3-baruch',15,2,$n$Revelation 14:13 — *Blessed are the dead which die in Yahusha (Lord) from henceforth: Yea, saith the Spirit, that they may rest from their labours; and their works do follow them.* The good works gathered into the full baskets are the works that follow the righteous and are rewarded.$n$,$n$And as for the angels which brought the baskets which were full, he filled them with oil, saying, Take it away, reward our friends an hundredfold, and those who have laboriously wrought good works.$n$,false),
(55277,'S','2-enoch',33,1,'2-enoch',33,1,$n$2 Peter 3:8 — *But, beloved, be not ignorant of this one thing, that one day is with Yahuah (Lord) as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day.* The "seventh thousand" and the eighth thousand of 2 Enoch 33:1 rest on the apostle's measure of a day as a thousand years before the Lord.$n$,$n$And I appointed the eighth day also, that the eighth day should be the first-created after my work, and that the first seven revolve in the form of the seventh thousand, and that at the beginning of the eighth thousand there should be a time of not-counting, endless, with neither years nor months nor weeks nor days nor hours.$n$,false),
(55409,'S','2-enoch',60,1,'2-enoch',60,1,$n$Genesis 9:6 — *Whoso sheddeth man's blood, by man shall his blood be shed: for in the image of Elohim (God) made he man.* "He who works the killing of a man’s soul, kills his own soul" is the word given Noah — the shedder of man's blood has his own blood shed, for man bears Elohim's image.$n$,$n$He who works the killing of a man’s soul, kills his own soul, and kills his own body, and there is no cure for him for all time.$n$,false),
(55426,'S','2-enoch',64,5,'2-enoch',64,5,$n$Genesis 5:24 — *And Enoch walked with Elohim (God): and he was not; for Elohim (God) took him.* The Enoch the people bless as one Yahuah "chose you, rather than all men on earth" in 2 Enoch 64:5 is the man Moses records as walking with Elohim and being taken — honored, not deified.$n$,$n$For you shalt be glorified before Yahuah's (Lord’s) face for all time, since Yahuah (Lord) chose you, rather than all men on earth, and designated you writer of all his creation, visible and invisible, and redeemed of the sins of man, and helper of your household.$n$,false),
(55434,'S','2-enoch',65,6,'2-enoch',65,6,$n$Revelation 22:5 — *And there shall be no night there; and they need no candle, neither light of the sun; for Yahuah Elohim (the Lord God) giveth them light: and they shall reign for ever and ever.* The "nor night, nor darkness, but great light" of 2 Enoch 65:6 is John's city where there is no night and Yahuah Himself is the light.$n$,$n$There will be one aeon, and all the righteous who shall escape Yahuah's (Lord’s) great judgment, shall be collected in the great aeon, for the righteous the great aeon will begin, and they will live eternally, and then too there will be amongst them neither labour, nor sickness, nor humiliation, nor anxiety, nor need, nor brutality, nor night, nor darkness, but great light.$n$,false),
(55437,'S','2-enoch',66,5,'2-enoch',66,5,$n$Psalms 139:8 — *If I ascend up into heaven, thou art there: if I make my bed in hell, behold, thou art there.* The "If you look to heaven, Yahuah Shammah (the Lord is there)... and all the under-earth, Yahuah Shammah (the Lord is there)" of 2 Enoch 66:5 is David's confession that Yahuah fills heaven and the depth alike.$n$,$n$If you look to heaven, Yahuah Shammah (the Lord is there); if you take thought of the sea’s deep and all the under-earth, Yahuah Shammah (the Lord is there).$n$,false),
(57887,'S','2-baruch',12,4,'2-baruch',12,4,$n$2 Peter 3:9 — *Yahuah (Lord) is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness; but is longsuffering to us-ward* — the 'long-suffering' that holds the wrath by reins, named by the apostle.$n$,$n$For assuredly in its own season shall the (divine) wrath awake against thee, Which now in long-suffering is held in as it were by reins.$n$,false),
(57889,'S','2-baruch',12,4,'2-baruch',12,4,$n$Habakkuk 2:3 — *For the vision is yet for an appointed time, but at the end it shall speak, and not lie: though it tarry, wait for it; because it will surely come* — the wrath that 'in its own season shall the (divine) wrath awake' the appointed delay Baruch describes.$n$,$n$For assuredly in its own season shall the (divine) wrath awake against thee, Which now in long-suffering is held in as it were by reins.$n$,false),
(57901,'S','2-baruch',14,12,'2-baruch',14,12,$n$Revelation 14:13 — *Blessed are the dead which die in Yahusha (Lord) from henceforth: Yea, saith the Spirit, that they may rest from their labours; and their works do follow them.* — the righteous departing without fear, their works 'preserved in treasuries.'$n$,$n$For the righteous justly hope for the end, and without fear depart from this habitation, because they have with Thee a store of works preserved in treasuries.$n$,false),
(57906,'S','2-baruch',14,8,'2-baruch',14,8,$n$Romans 11:33 — *O the depth of the riches both of the wisdom and knowledge of Elohim (God)! how unsearchable are his judgments, and his ways past finding out!* — Baruch's 'who, O Yahuah (LORD), my Lord, will comprehend Thy judgement' in the apostle's very words.$n$,$n$But who, O Yahuah (LORD), my Lord, will comprehend Thy judgement, Or who will search out the profoundness of Thy way? Or who will think out the [weight] of Thy path?$n$,false),
(57950,'S','2-baruch',26,1,'2-baruch',26,1,$n$Revelation 6:10 — *And they cried with a loud voice, saying, How long, O Yahuah (Lord), holy and true, dost thou not judge and avenge our blood on them that dwell on the earth?* Baruch's question whether the tribulation will continue many years is the same "how long" the martyred souls cry under the altar.$n$,$n$And I answered and said: 'Will that tribulation which is to be continue a long time, and will that necessity embrace many years?'$n$,false),
(57962,'S','2-baruch',29,8,'2-baruch',29,8,$n$*And it shall come to pass at that self-same time that the treasury of manna shall again descend from on high, and they will eat of it in those years, because these are they who have come to the consummation of time.* (2 Baruch 29:8). *And Yahusha (Jesus) said unto them, I am the bread of life: he that cometh to me shall never hunger; and he that believeth on me shall never thirst.* (John 6:35). In the years of the Messiah, 2 Baruch says, the treasury of manna will again descend from on high, and they will eat of it. The bread that came down for the tribes in the wilderness is promised again for the end of time. Yahusha (Jesus) says of himself that he is the bread of life, and that the one who comes to him shall never hunger and the one who believes on him shall never thirst. The bread from on high that Baruch looks for is the one standing before them in John.$n$,$n$And it shall come to pass at that self-same time that the treasury of manna shall again descend from on high, and they will eat of it in those years, because these are they who have come to the consummation of time.$n$,true),
(57979,'S','2-baruch',30,2,'2-baruch',30,2,$n$1 Thessalonians 4:16 — *For Yahusha (Lord) himself shall descend from heaven with a shout, with the voice of the archangel, and with the trump of Elohim (God): and the dead in Messiah (Christ) shall rise first:* That those asleep in hope of Him rise again at His glorious return is Paul's word that at the descent from heaven the dead in Messiah rise first.$n$,$n$Then all who have fallen asleep in hope of Him shall rise again. And it shall come to pass at that time that the treasuries will be opened in which is preserved the number of the souls of the righteous, and they shall come forth, and a multitude of souls shall be seen together in one assemblage of one thought, and the first shall rejoice and the last shall not be grieved.$n$,false),
(58009,'S','2-baruch',37,1,'2-baruch',37,1,$n$2 Thessalonians 2:8 — *whom Yahusha (Lord) shall consume with the spirit of his mouth, and shall destroy with the brightness of his coming:* — the last wicked one burned away before the reign that grows in peace.$n$,$n$And after these things I saw that cedar burning, and the vine growing, itself and all around it, the plain full of unfading flowers. And I indeed awoke and arose.$n$,false),
(58029,'S','2-baruch',40,2,'2-baruch',40,2,$n$2 Thess 2:8 — *And then shall that Wicked be revealed, whom Yahusha (Lord) shall consume with the spirit of his mouth, and shall destroy with the brightness of his coming:* — the lawless one slain by the Messiah's word, the same convicting-and-slaying Baruch describes.$n$,$n$And afterwards he will put him to death, and protect the rest of My people which shall be found in the place which I have chosen.$n$,false),
(58066,'S','2-baruch',48,9,'2-baruch',48,9,$n$Rom 4:17 — *even Elohim (God), who quickeneth the dead, and calleth those things which be not as though they were.* — with a word He quickens that which was not.$n$,$n$With nods of fear and indignation Thou commandest the flames, And they change into spirits, And with a word Thou quickenest that which was not, And with mighty power Thou holdest that which has not yet come.$n$,false),
(58080,'S','2-baruch',51,4,'2-baruch',51,4,$n$Rom 2:13 — *For not the hearers of the law are just before Elohim (God), but the doers of the law shall be justified.* — the lost stopped their ears against the law and so were condemned.$n$,$n$For over this above all shall those who come then lament, that they rejected My law, and stopped their ears that they might not hear wisdom or receive understanding.$n$,false),
(58136,'S','2-baruch',61,7,'2-baruch',61,7,$n$1 Chr 22:9 — *who shall be a man of rest; and I will give him rest from all his enemies round about: for his name shall be Solomon, and I will give peace and quietness unto Yashar'el (Israel) in his days.* — Solomon, the man of rest, in whose days the land was beloved and glorified, as Baruch tells.$n$,$n$And the land [which] was then beloved by Yahuah (Lord), And because its inhabitants sinned not, it was glorified beyond all lands, And the city Zion ruled then over all lands and regions.$n$,false),
(58216,'S','2-baruch',74,2,'2-baruch',74,2,$n$*For that time is the consummation of that which is corruptible, And the beginning of that which is not corruptible. Therefore those things which were predicted shall belong to it: Therefore it is far away from evils, and near to those things which die not.* (2 Baruch 74:2–3) *And Elohim (God) shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain: for the former things are passed away.* (Revelation 21:4) John sees the same turning in Revelation. When the corruptible reaches its end the incorruptible begins, and Baruch says that age is far from evils and near to those things which die not, which is what John means when there is no more death. Elohim (God) wipes the tears away because the former things have passed, and both writers are looking at the same line between this age and the one that does not end.$n$,$n$For that time is the consummation of that which is corruptible, And the beginning of that which is not corruptible.$n$,true),
(58270,'S','2-baruch',85,12,'2-baruch',85,12,$n$2 Cor 6:2 — *behold, now is the accepted time; behold, now is the day of salvation.* — the open day of repentance Baruch says will not return once the age is past, so turn now.$n$,$n$For lo! when the El Elyon (Most High) will bring to pass all these things, There shall not there be again [a place of repentance, nor] a limit to the times, Nor a duration for the hours, Nor a change of ways, Nor place for prayer, Nor sending of petitions, Nor receiving of knowledge, Nor giving of love, Nor place of repentance for the soul, Nor supplication for offences, Nor intercession of the fathers, Nor prayer of the prophets, Nor help of the righteous.$n$,false),
(59929,'S','testaments-xii',9,9,'testaments-xii',9,9,$n$Gen 37:27 — *Come, and let us sell him to the Ishmeelites, and let not our hand be upon him; for he is our brother and our flesh. And his brethren were content.* — Judah's counsel that Simeon recalls, "Yahudah (Judah) my brother sold him to the Ishmaelites."$n$,$n$For when I went to Shechem to bring ointment for the flocks, and Reuben to Dothan, where were our necessaries and all our stores, Yahudah (Judah) my brother sold him to the Ishmaelites.$n$,false),
(59935,'S','testaments-xii',10,4,'testaments-xii',10,4,$n$Prov 14:27 — *The fear of Yahuah (LORD) is a fountain of life, to depart from the snares of death.* — the very deliverance Simeon found: "deliverance from envy cometh by the fear of Elohim (God)."$n$,$n$Two years 'therefore' I afflicted my soul with fasting in the fear of Yahuah (Lord), and I learnt that deliverance from envy cometh by the fear of Elohim (God).$n$,false),
(59936,'S','testaments-xii',10,3,'testaments-xii',10,2,$n$James 3:16 — *For where envying and strife is, there is confusion and every evil work.* — envy's fruit, the same root Simeon names that "suffereth him 'neither to eat nor to drink', nor to do any good thing."$n$,$n$For envy ruleth over the whole mind of a man, and suffereth him 'neither to eat nor to drink', nor to do any good thing.$n$,false),
(59944,'S','testaments-xii',12,6,'testaments-xii',12,6,$n$Zech 6:13 — *and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.* — the division "in Levi and Yahudah (Judah)," priest and king at peace, that Simeon names.$n$,$n$And they shall be few in number, divided in Levi and Yahudah (Judah), and there shall be none of you for sovereignty, even as also our father prophesied in his blessings.$n$,false),
(59946,'S','testaments-xii',12,3,'testaments-xii',12,3,$n$Gen 6:11 — *The earth also was corrupt before Elohim (God), and the earth was filled with violence.* — fornication "mother of all evils," filling the earth with corruption as in Noah's day.$n$,$n$Beware, therefore, of fornication, For fornication is mother of all evils, Separating from Elohim (God), and bringing near to Beliar.$n$,false),
(59947,'S','testaments-xii',12,3,'testaments-xii',12,3,$n$Gen 6:2 — *That the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair; and they took them wives of all which they chose.* — the fornication of the Watchers that "bringing near to Beliar," the root Enoch expounds.$n$,$n$Beware, therefore, of fornication, For fornication is mother of all evils, Separating from Elohim (God), and bringing near to Beliar.$n$,false),
(59952,'S','testaments-xii',13,5,'testaments-xii',13,5,$n$Gen 9:26 — *Blessed be Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) of Shem; and Canaan shall be his servant.* — "the Mighty One of Yashar'el (Israel) shall glorify Shem" and Canaan perish, Noah's blessing fulfilled.$n$,$n$Then the Mighty One of Yashar'el (Israel) shall glorify Shem, For Yahuah Elohim (the Lord God) shall appear on earth, And save the sons of men.$n$,false),
(59956,'S','testaments-xii',14,2,'testaments-xii',14,2,$n$Heb 7:25 — *Wherefore he is able also to save them to the uttermost that come unto Elohim (God) by him, seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.* — "He shall save all [the Gentiles and] the race of Yashar'el (Israel)," the salvation arising from the two tribes.$n$,$n$For Yahuah (Lord) shall raise up from Levi as it were a High-priest, and from Yahudah (Judah) as it were a King [Elohim (God) and man], He shall save all [the Gentiles and] the race of Yashar'el (Israel).$n$,false),
(59968,'S','testaments-xii',18,7,'testaments-xii',18,7,$n$2 Enoch 3:1 — *bore him up on to the first heaven and placed him on the clouds ... and showed me a very great Sea, greater than the earthly sea.* Enoch's ascent to the first heaven and its great sea is the same first heaven and "great sea hanging" Levi enters.$n$,$n$And I entered from the first heaven, and I saw there a great sea hanging.$n$,false),
(59974,'S','testaments-xii',19,8,'testaments-xii',19,8,$n$Isaiah 6:3 — *Holy, holy, holy, is Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts): the whole earth is full of his glory.* The thrones and dominions that 'always they offer praise to Elohim (God)' echo the seraphim's unceasing cry.$n$,$n$And in [the heaven next to this] are thrones and dominions, in which always they offer praise to Elohim (God).$n$,false),
(59977,'S','testaments-xii',20,3,'testaments-xii',20,3,$n$Isaiah 9:2 — *The people that walked in darkness have seen a great light.* Levi lighting 'The light of knowledge shalt thou light up in Jacob' and shining 'as the sun shalt thou be to all the seed of Yashar'el (Israel)' is the great light upon the people.$n$,$n$The light of knowledge shalt thou light up in Jacob, And as the sun shalt thou be to all the seed of Yashar'el (Israel).$n$,false),
(59982,'S','testaments-xii',21,2,'testaments-xii',21,2,$n$Malachi 3:1 — *Yahuah (Lord), whom ye seek, shall suddenly come to his temple.* 'until I come and sojourn in the midst of Yashar'el (Israel)' is the Lord's promised coming to His temple.$n$,$n$And He said to me: Levi, I have given thee the blessings of the priesthood until I come and sojourn in the midst of Yashar'el (Israel).$n$,false),
(59986,'S','testaments-xii',24,11,'testaments-xii',24,11,$n$Hebrews 7:12 — *For the priesthood being changed, there is made of necessity a change also of the law.* That Levi's seed is divided 'for a sign of the glory of Yahuah (Lord) who is to come' answers to the changed priesthood Hebrews names.$n$,$n$And they said to me: Levi, thy seed shall be divided into three offices, for a sign of the glory of Yahuah (Lord) who is to come.$n$,false),
(60002,'S','testaments-xii',29,5,'testaments-xii',29,5,$n$Matthew 6:20 — *But lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust doth corrupt.* 'Work righteousness... That ye may have (it) as a treasure in heaven' is the treasure laid up above.$n$,$n$Work righteousness, therefore, my children, upon the earth, That ye may have (it) as a treasure in heaven.$n$,false),
(60003,'S','testaments-xii',29,1,'testaments-xii',29,1,$n$Deuteronomy 6:5 — *And thou shalt love Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) with all thine heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy might.* 'Fear Yahuah Elohaychem (the Lord your God) with your whole heart' is the Shema's command of whole-hearted love.$n$,$n$And now, my children, I command you: Fear Yahuah Elohaychem (the Lord your God) with your whole heart, And walk in simplicity according to all His law.$n$,false),
(60006,'S','testaments-xii',30,7,'testaments-xii',30,7,$n$Malachi 2:7 — *the priest's lips should keep knowledge, and they should seek the law at his mouth: for he is the messenger of Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts).* The office the priests forsake when 'puffed up because of your priesthood' is the lips that should keep knowledge.$n$,$n$And ye shall be puffed up because of your priesthood, lifting yourselves up against men, and not only so, but also against the commands of Elohim (God).$n$,false),
(60017,'S','testaments-xii',34,10,'testaments-xii',34,10,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* 'he shall open the gates of paradise, And shall remove the threatening sword against Adam' undoes the flaming sword that barred Eden.$n$,$n$And he shall open the gates of paradise, And shall remove the threatening sword against Adam.$n$,false),
(60026,'S','testaments-xii',34,2,'testaments-xii',34,2,$n$Psalm 110:4 — *Yahuah (LORD) hath sworn, and will not repent, Thou art a priest for ever after the order of Melek Tsadiq (Melchizedek).* The new priest Yahuah (the Lord) raises up, to whom all his words are revealed and who judges the earth for a multitude of days, is the priest Yahuah (the LORD) swore in after the order of Melek Tsadiq (Melchizedek) — a priesthood not from Levi's line and not for a season.$n$,$n$Then shall Yahuah (Lord) raise up a new priest. And to him all the words of Yahuah (Lord) shall be revealed; And he shall execute a righteous judgment upon the earth for a multitude of days.$n$,false),
(60027,'S','testaments-xii',35,3,'testaments-xii',35,3,$n$Deuteronomy 30:19 — *I call heaven and earth to record this day against you... therefore choose life.* 'Yahuah (Lord) is witness, and His angels are witnesses, and ye are witnesses' is Moses' calling of heaven and earth to record the choice of life.$n$,$n$And their father said unto them, Yahuah (Lord) is witness, and His angels are witnesses, and ye are witnesses, and I am witness, concerning the word of your mouth. And his sons said unto him: We are witnesses.$n$,false),
(60028,'S','testaments-xii',35,1,'testaments-xii',35,1,$n$Deuteronomy 30:15 — *See, I have set before thee this day life and good, and death and evil.* 'choose, therefore, for yourselves either the light or the darkness, either the law of Yahuah (Lord) or the works of Beliar' is the life-and-death Moses set before Israel.$n$,$n$And now, my children, ye have heard all; choose, therefore, for yourselves either the light or the darkness, either the law of Yahuah (Lord) or the works of Beliar.$n$,false),
(60042,'S','testaments-xii',47,5,'testaments-xii',47,5,$n$Genesis 38:26 — *And Yahudah (Judah) acknowledged them, and said, She hath been more righteous than I; because that I gave her not to Shelah my son. And he knew her again no more.* Judah's "she privily sent my pledges, and put me to shame" is the same confession Moses sets down.$n$,$n$And not knowing what I had done, I wished to slay her; but she privily sent my pledges, and put me to shame.$n$,false),
(60057,'S','testaments-xii',52,6,'testaments-xii',52,6,$n$Genesis 49:10 — *The sceptre shall not depart from Yahudah (Judah), nor a lawgiver from between his feet, until Shiloh come; and unto him shall the gathering of the people be.* The kingdom "from me shall the kingdom be established" is the scepter Jacob fixed on Judah.$n$,$n$And I know that from me shall the kingdom be established.$n$,false),
(60075,'S','testaments-xii',57,2,'testaments-xii',57,2,$n$Isaiah 45:17 — *But Yashar'el (Israel) shall be saved in Yahuah (LORD) with an everlasting salvation: ye shall not be ashamed nor confounded world without end.* The coming "salvation of Yashar'el (Israel)" and rest in peace is Isaiah's everlasting salvation.$n$,$n$And among men of another race shall my kingdom be brought to an end, Until the salvation of Yashar'el (Israel) shall come, 'Until the appearing of the Elohim (God) of righteousness,' That Jacob [and all the Gentiles] may rest in peace.$n$,false),
(60076,'S','testaments-xii',57,2,'testaments-xii',57,2,$n$Genesis 49:10 — *The sceptre shall not depart from Yahudah (Judah), nor a lawgiver from between his feet, until Shiloh come; and unto him shall the gathering of the people be.* The kingdom held "Until the salvation of Yashar'el (Israel) shall come" is the scepter held until Shiloh comes.$n$,$n$And among men of another race shall my kingdom be brought to an end, Until the salvation of Yashar'el (Israel) shall come, 'Until the appearing of the Elohim (God) of righteousness,' That Jacob [and all the Gentiles] may rest in peace.$n$,false),
(60085,'S','testaments-xii',59,4,'testaments-xii',59,4,$n$Isaiah 11:1 — *And there shall come forth a rod out of the stem of Jesse, and a Branch shall grow out of his roots.* "This Branch of Elohim (God) El Elyon (Most High)" is Isaiah's Branch grown from the roots of Jesse.$n$,$n$[This Branch of Elohim (God) El Elyon (Most High), And this Fountain giving life unto all.]$n$,false),
(60091,'S','testaments-xii',59,1,'testaments-xii',59,1,$n$Numbers 24:17 — *...there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel), and shall smite the corners of Moab, and destroy all the children of Sheth.* Judah's "shall a star arise to you from Jacob" is Balaam's very oracle of the Star and Sceptre.$n$,$n$And after these things shall a star arise to you from Jacob in peace, And a man shall arise [from my seed], like the sun of righteousness, Walking with the sons of men in meekness and righteousness; And no sin shall be found in him.$n$,false),
(60113,'S','testaments-xii',66,7,'testaments-xii',66,7,$n$Genesis 49:10 — *The sceptre shall not depart from Yahudah (Judah), nor a lawgiver from between his feet, until Shiloh come; and unto him shall the gathering of the people be.* "to Yahudah (Judah) the kingdom" is Jacob's own dying word over Judah's sceptre.$n$,$n$And Levi and Yahudah (Judah) were glorified by Yahuah (Lord) even among the sons of Jacob; for Yahuah (Lord) gave them an inheritance, and to Levi He gave the priesthood, and to Yahudah (Judah) the kingdom.$n$,false),
(60116,'S','testaments-xii',66,1,'testaments-xii',66,1,$n$Matthew 22:40 — *On these two commandments hang all the law and the prophets.* Issachar's "Keep, therefore, my children, the law of Elohim (God)" reduced to love of God and neighbour is the very hinge the Master names.$n$,$n$Keep, therefore, my children, the law of Elohim (God), And get singleness, 'And walk in guilelessness, Not playing the busybody with the business of your neighbour.$n$,false),
(60154,'S','testaments-xii',76,1,'testaments-xii',76,1,$n$Matthew 5:7 — *Blessed are the merciful: for they shall obtain mercy.* "Have, therefore, yourselves also, my children, compassion... that Yahuah (Lord) also may have compassion and mercy upon you" is the Beatitude almost word for word.$n$,$n$Have, therefore, yourselves also, my children, compassion towards every man with mercy, that Yahuah (Lord) also may have compassion and mercy upon you.$n$,false),
(60162,'S','testaments-xii',77,5,'testaments-xii',77,5,$n$Ezekiel 37:22 — *And I will make them one nation in the land upon the mountains of Yashar'el (Israel); and one king shall be king to them all: and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all.* Zebulun's "Ye shall be divided in Yashar'el (Israel), And ye shall follow two kings" is the very division of the two kingdoms Ezekiel says shall at last be made one.$n$,$n$For I have learnt in the writing of my fathers, that Ye shall be divided in Yashar'el (Israel), And ye shall follow two kings, And shall work every abomination.$n$,false),
(60179,'S','testaments-xii',83,13,'testaments-xii',83,13,$n$Ezek 37:27 — *My tabernacle also shall be with them: yea, I will be their Elohim (God), and they shall be my people.* The Lord in the midst of His restored city, exactly as Dan promises Jerusalem.$n$,$n$And no longer shall Jerusalem endure desolation, Nor Yashar'el (Israel) be led captive; For Yahuah (Lord) shall be in the midst of it [living amongst men], And the Holy One of Yashar'el (Israel) shall reign over it [in humility and in poverty; and he who believeth on Him shall reign amongst men in truth].$n$,false),
(60185,'S','testaments-xii',83,12,'testaments-xii',83,12,$n$Rev 21:2 — *And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from Elohim (God) out of heaven*. The very New Jerusalem in which Dan says the righteous shall rejoice.$n$,$n$And the saints shall rest in Eden, And in the New Jerusalem will the righteous rejoice, And it shall be unto the glory of Elohim (God) for ever.$n$,false),
(60186,'S','testaments-xii',83,11,'testaments-xii',83,11,$n$Rev 20:6 — *but they shall be priests of Elohim (God) and of Messiah (Christ), and shall reign with him a thousand years.* The saints whose captivity is taken from Beliar, reigning in the peace Dan promises them.$n$,$n$And the captivity shall he take from Beliar [the souls of the saints], And turn disobedient hearts unto Yahuah (Lord), And give to them that call upon him eternal peace.$n$,false),
(60190,'S','testaments-xii',83,10,'testaments-xii',83,10,$n$Num 24:17 — *there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel)*. Balaam's Sceptre, the king from Judah whom Dan joins with Levi as the salvation of the Lord.$n$,$n$And there shall arise unto you from the tribe of [Yahudah (Judah) and of] Levi the salvation of Yahuah (Lord); And he shall make war against Beliar, And execute an everlasting vengeance on our enemies;$n$,false),
(60192,'S','testaments-xii',84,7,'testaments-xii',84,7,$n$Deut 30:4 — *from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee, and from thence will he fetch thee:* The Lord's name in every place of Israel and among the Gentiles — the gathering of the scattered Dan foresees.$n$,$n$And His name shall be in every place of Yashar'el (Israel), 'and among the Gentiles'.$n$,false),
(60194,'S','testaments-xii',84,4,'testaments-xii',84,4,$n$Deut 30:2 — *And shalt return unto Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), and shalt obey his voice according to all that I command thee this day, thou and thy children, with all thine heart*. The day of Israel's repentance on which Dan says the enemy's kingdom ends.$n$,$n$For he knoweth that on the day on which Yashar'el (Israel) shall repent, the kingdom of the enemy shall be brought to an end.$n$,false),
(60196,'S','testaments-xii',84,2,'testaments-xii',84,2,$n$1 Tim 2:5 — *For there is one Elohim (God), and one mediator between Elohim (God) and men, the man HaMashiach Yahusha (Christ Jesus);* The single mediator Dan tells his sons to draw near to — the appointed Anointed, not a co-equal, but the man who stands between God and Israel.$n$,$n$Draw near unto Elohim (God) and to the angel that intercedeth for you, for he is a mediator between Elohim (God) and man, and for the peace of Yashar'el (Israel) he shall stand up against the kingdom of the enemy.$n$,false),
(60202,'S','testaments-xii',87,8,'testaments-xii',87,8,$n$Genesis 1:31 — *And Elohim (God) saw every thing that he had made, and, behold, it was very good. And the evening and the morning were the sixth day.* — "Elohim (God) made all things good in their order" echoes the verdict over the whole creation, that it was very good.$n$,$n$'For' Elohim (God) made all things good in their order, the five senses in the head, and He joined on the neck to the head, adding to it the hair also for comeliness and glory, then the heart for understanding, the belly for excrement, and the stomach for grinding, the windpipe for taking in (the breath), the liver for wrath, the gall for bitterness, the spleen for laughter, the reins 'for prudence, the muscles of the loins' for power, the lungs for drawing in, the loins for strength, and so forth.$n$,false),
(60205,'S','testaments-xii',87,5,'testaments-xii',87,3,$n$Psalm 139:14 — *I will praise thee; for I am fearfully and wonderfully made: marvellous are thy works; and that my soul knoweth right well.* — that the body is made "by weight, and measure, and rule" after the likeness of the spirit is the wonder of being fearfully and wonderfully made.$n$,$n$And the one does not fall short of the other by a third part of a hair; for by weight, and measure, and rule was all the creation made.$n$,false),
(60216,'S','testaments-xii',88,2,'testaments-xii',88,2,$n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple.* — "change not the law of Elohim (God)" rests on the law that is perfect, the same psalm that begins with the ordered heavens.$n$,$n$Sun and moon and stars change not their order; so do ye also change not the law of Elohim (God) in the disorderliness of your doings.$n$,false),
(60219,'S','testaments-xii',89,5,'testaments-xii',89,3,$n$Isaiah 11:11 — *And it shall come to pass in that day, that Yahuah (Lord) shall set his hand again the second time to recover the remnant of his people, which shall be left...* — "after ye have become minished and made few, ye shall return" is the remnant the LORD recovers the second time.$n$,$n$And after ye have become minished and made few, ye shall return and acknowledge Yahuah Elohaychem (the Lord your God); and He shall bring you back into your own land, according to His abundant mercy.$n$,false),
(60221,'S','testaments-xii',89,3,'testaments-xii',89,3,$n$Deuteronomy 30:3 — *That then Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) will turn thy captivity, and have compassion upon thee, and will return and gather thee from all the nations, whither Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) hath scattered thee.* — "ye shall return and acknowledge Yahuah Elohaychem (the Lord your God); and He shall bring you back into your own land, according to His abundant mercy" is the turning of the captivity and the gathering Moses promised.$n$,$n$And after ye have become minished and made few, ye shall return and acknowledge Yahuah Elohaychem (the Lord your God); and He shall bring you back into your own land, according to His abundant mercy.$n$,false),
(60233,'S','testaments-xii',93,10,'testaments-xii',93,10,$n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple.* — "Be ye therefore wise in Elohim (God)... understanding the order of His commandments" rests on the law that is perfect and makes the simple wise.$n$,$n$Be ye therefore wise in Elohim (God), 'my children,' and prudent, understanding the order of His commandments, and the laws of every word, that Yahuah (Lord) may love you.$n$,false),
(60235,'S','testaments-xii',93,3,'testaments-xii',93,3,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* — "Elohim (God) shall appear, dwelling among men on earth" is fulfilled when the Word was made flesh and dwelt among us — the only begotten whom the Father sent, the Formed one walking among men.$n$,$n$For through their tribes shall Elohim (God) appear [dwelling among men] on earth, To save the race of Yashar'el (Israel), And to gather together the righteous from amongst the Gentiles.$n$,false),
(60239,'S','testaments-xii',93,3,'testaments-xii',93,3,$n$Zechariah 2:10 — *Sing and rejoice, O daughter of Zion: for, lo, I come, and I will dwell in the midst of thee, saith Yahuah (LORD).* — "shall Elohim (God) appear [dwelling among men] on earth" is the LORD's own promise to come and dwell in the midst of Zion.$n$,$n$For through their tribes shall Elohim (God) appear [dwelling among men] on earth, To save the race of Yashar'el (Israel), And to gather together the righteous from amongst the Gentiles.$n$,false),
(60274,'S','testaments-xii',101,1,'testaments-xii',101,1,$n$Psalms 37:1 — *Fret not thyself because of evildoers, neither be thou envious against the workers of iniquity.* Gad's 'do not be vexed... be not envious' when another prospers is David's own counsel against envy.$n$,$n$If a man prospereth more than you, do not be vexed, but pray also for him, that he may have perfect 'prosperity.' For so it is expedient for you.$n$,false),
(60288,'S','testaments-xii',104,9,'testaments-xii',104,9,$n$Leviticus 11:6 — *And the hare, because he cheweth the cud, but divideth not the hoof; he is unclean unto you.* Asher's "half clean, but in very deed are unclean" hare is the very creature Moses names: it answers one mark of cleanness and fails the other, like the double-faced man.$n$,$n$Such men are hares; for they are half clean, but in very deed are unclean.$n$,false),
(60307,'S','testaments-xii',109,1,'testaments-xii',109,1,$n$Genesis 19:24 — *Then Yahuah (LORD) rained upon Sodom and upon Gomorrah brimstone and fire from Yahuah (LORD) out of heaven;* Asher's warning, "Become not, my children, as Sodom, which knew not the angels of Yahuah (Lord), and perished for ever," recalls the city that rejected the two angels and was destroyed.$n$,$n$Become not, my children, as Sodom, which knew not the angels of Yahuah (Lord), and perished for ever.$n$,false),
(60310,'S','testaments-xii',111,4,'testaments-xii',111,4,$n$Genesis 39:2 — *And Yahuah (LORD) was with Joseph, and he was a prosperous man; and he was in the house of his master the Egyptian.* The refrain of the whole testament — "Yahuah (Lord) loved me... the Elohim (God) of my fathers guarded me" — is Moses' own refrain over Joseph.$n$,$n$These my brethren hated me, but Yahuah (Lord) loved me: They wished to slay me, but the Elohim (God) of my fathers guarded me: They let me down into a pit, and the El Elyon (Most High) brought me up again.$n$,false),
(60319,'S','testaments-xii',113,3,'testaments-xii',113,3,$n$2 Timothy 2:22 — *Flee also youthful lusts: but follow righteousness, faith, charity, peace, with them that call on Yahusha (Lord) out of a pure heart.* Joseph's weeping, praying, and fasting is exactly the fleeing of youthful lust by calling on the Lord that Paul charges Timothy.$n$,$n$But I remembered the words of my father, and going into my chamber, 'I wept and' prayed unto Yahuah (Lord).$n$,false),
(60321,'S','testaments-xii',113,1,'testaments-xii',113,1,$n$Genesis 39:10 — *And it came to pass, as she spake to Joseph day by day, that he hearkened not unto her, to lie by her, or to be with her.* The woman's repeated threatening "How often did the Egyptian woman threaten me with death!... and then call me back and threaten me" is Moses' "day by day."$n$,$n$How often did the Egyptian woman threaten me with death! How often did she give me over to punishment, and then call me back and threaten me, and when I was unwilling to company with her, she said to me:$n$,false),
(60332,'S','testaments-xii',119,2,'testaments-xii',119,2,$n$2 Timothy 2:22 — *Flee also youthful lusts: but follow righteousness, faith, charity, peace, with them that call on Yahusha (Lord) out of a pure heart.* That God loves him "who in a den of darkness combines fasting with chastity" over the man of luxury and licence is Paul's same preference of righteousness over youthful lust.$n$,$n$And not even in thought did I incline unto her. For Elohim (God) loveth him who in a den of darkness combines fasting with chastity, rather than the man who in kings' chambers combines luxury with licence.$n$,false),
(60338,'S','testaments-xii',125,3,'testaments-xii',125,3,$n$Genesis 45:1 — *Then Joseph could not refrain himself before all them that stood by him; and he cried, Cause every man to go out from me.* That Joseph here "desired greatly to weep, but I restrained myself" is the same overflowing heart Moses records breaking forth before his brethren.$n$,$n$'When I heard this my bowels were dissolved and my heart melted', and I desired greatly to weep, but I restrained myself, that I should not put my brethren to shame. 'And I said unto them, I know not, I am a slave'.$n$,false),
(60339,'S','testaments-xii',127,2,'testaments-xii',127,2,$n$Leviticus 19:18 — *Thou shalt not avenge, nor bear any grudge against the children of thy people, but thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am Yahuah (LORD).* "love one another, and with long-suffering hide 'ye one another's faults'" is the royal commandment in plain words.$n$,$n$Do ye also, therefore, love one another, and with long-suffering hide 'ye one another's faults'.$n$,false),
(60361,'S','testaments-xii',132,3,'testaments-xii',132,3,$n$Gen 37:28 — *and sold Joseph to the Ishmeelites for twenty pieces of silver: and they brought Joseph into Egypt.* — the very sale Joseph names, "they gave me to the Ishmaelites."$n$,$n$And he said unto me: Even so, brother, when they had stripped me of my coat they gave me to the Ishmaelites, and they gave me a loin cloth, and scourged me, and bade me run.$n$,false),
(60364,'S','testaments-xii',133,8,'testaments-xii',133,8,$n$*In thee shall be fulfilled the prophecy of heaven [concerning the Lamb of Elohim (God), and Saviour of the world], that a blameless one shall be delivered up for lawless men, and a sinless shall die for ungodly men [in the blood of the covenant, for the salvation of the Gentiles and 'of Israel', and shall destroy Beliar and his servants].* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 133:8). *For Messiah (Christ) also hath once suffered for sins, the just for the unjust, that he might bring us to Elohim (God), being put to death in the flesh, but quickened by the Spirit:* (1 Peter 3:18). Jacob, embracing Joseph, says that in him the prophecy of heaven will be fulfilled: a blameless one delivered up for lawless men and a sinless one dying for ungodly men. Peter says it of the Messiah (Christ), who suffered once for sins, the just for the unjust, so that He might bring us to Elohim (God). The two lines carry the same shape, the righteous one giving himself for those who are not, and the end of it is bringing the lost home to the Father.$n$,$n$In thee shall be fulfilled the prophecy of heaven [concerning the Lamb of Elohim (God), and Saviour of the world], that a blameless one shall be delivered up for lawless men, and a sinless shall die for ungodly men [in the blood of the covenant, for the salvation of the Gentiles and 'of Israel', and shall destroy Beliar and his servants].$n$,true),
(60366,'S','testaments-xii',133,6,'testaments-xii',133,6,$n$*For Joseph also besought our father 'that he would pray for his brethren', that 'the Lord' would not impute to them as sin whatever evil they had done unto him.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 133:6). *But I say unto you, Love your enemies, bless them that curse you, do good to them that hate you, and pray for them which despitefully use you, and persecute you;* (Matthew 5:44). His brothers had done Joseph evil, and Joseph asked their father to pray for them and that Yahuah (the Lord) would not count it to them as sin. That is Matthew 5:44 lived before it was spoken: praying for those who despitefully use you and persecute you. Benjamin hands the story to his sons as proof that loving an enemy can be done, even when the enemy is your own brother.$n$,$n$For Joseph also besought our father 'that he would pray for his brethren', that 'the Lord' would not impute to them as sin whatever evil they had done unto him.$n$,true),
(60397,'S','testaments-xii',139,3,'testaments-xii',139,3,$n$Deut 21:23 — *for he that is hanged is accursed of Elohim (God)* — the Torah's word on the one hanged on a tree, the curse the lifted-up Lord bears.$n$,$n$[And He shall enter into the [first] temple, and there shall Yahuah (Lord) be treated with outrage, and He shall be lifted up upon a tree.$n$,false),
(60421,'S','testaments-xii',141,1,'testaments-xii',141,1,$n$Deut 30:4 — *from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee, and from thence will he fetch thee.* — the gathering of "all Yashar'el (Israel) shall be gathered unto Yahuah (Lord)" Benjamin foresees.$n$,$n$If ye 'therefore, my children', walk in holiness 'according to the commandments of the Lord', ye shall again dwell securely with me, and all Yashar'el (Israel) shall be gathered unto Yahuah (Lord). And I shall no longer be called a ravening wolf on account of your ravages, but [a worker of Yahuah (Lord) distributing food to them that work what is good.$n$,false),
(177476,'T','testaments-xii',140,8,'testaments-xii',140,8,$n$*'And' then shall ye see Enoch, Noah, and Shem, and Abraham, and Isaac, and Jacob, rising on the right hand in gladness. Then shall we also rise, each one over our tribe, worshipping the King of heaven... Then also all men shall rise, some unto glory and some unto shame. And Yahuah (Lord) shall judge Yashar'el (Israel) first, for their unrighteousness... And then shall He judge all the Gentiles...* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 140:6–9). John sees *the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God)... and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works* (Revelation 20:12). Benjamin's *all men shall rise, some unto glory and some unto shame* is that standing of small and great: the rising first, then the judging.$n$,$n$Then also all men shall rise, some unto glory and some unto shame. And Yahuah (Lord) shall judge Yashar'el (Israel) first, for their unrighteousness; [for when He appeared as Elohim (God) in the flesh to deliver them they believed Him not].$n$,false),
(177477,'T','testaments-xii',140,8,'testaments-xii',140,8,$n$*'And' then shall ye see Enoch, Noah, and Shem, and Abraham, and Isaac, and Jacob, rising on the right hand in gladness. Then shall we also rise, each one over our tribe, worshipping the King of heaven... Then also all men shall rise, some unto glory and some unto shame. And Yahuah (Lord) shall judge Yashar'el (Israel) first, for their unrighteousness... And then shall He judge all the Gentiles...* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 140:6–9). Benjamin sets the rising in order: the fathers first, then the sons each over his tribe, and last *all men shall rise, some unto glory and some unto shame,* and then the judging. Revelation names that last hour: *the time of the dead, that they should be judged* (Revelation 11:18). The fathers and the tribes rise before; the rising of all men, to glory or to shame, comes at the time of the dead, when the one judgment is set.$n$,$n$Then also all men shall rise, some unto glory and some unto shame. And Yahuah (Lord) shall judge Yashar'el (Israel) first, for their unrighteousness; [for when He appeared as Elohim (God) in the flesh to deliver them they believed Him not].$n$,false),
(177478,'T','testaments-xii',60,1,'testaments-xii',60,1,$n$*And after these things shall Abraham and Isaac and Jacob arise unto life, and I and my brethren shall be chiefs of the tribes 'of Israel': Levi first, I the second, Joseph third, Benjamin fourth, Simeon fifth, Issachar sixth, and so all in order... And ye shall be the people of Yahuah (Lord), and have one tongue; And there shall be there no spirit of deceit of 'Beliar', For he shall be cast into the fire for ever. And they who have died in grief shall arise 'in joy', 'And they who were poor for Yahuah's (Lord's) sake shall be made rich,' And they who are put to death for Yahuah's (Lord's) sake shall awake 'to life'.* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 60:1, 3–4). John sees *the souls of them that were beheaded for the witness of Yahusha (Jesus)... and they lived and reigned with Messiah (Christ) a thousand years* (Revelation 20:4). Judah's testament holds the same rising: the fathers *arise unto life,* the sons stand as *chiefs of the tribes* *all in order,* and *they who are put to death for Yahuah's (Lord's) sake shall awake 'to life'.* The first resurrection raises the fathers and the faithful slain into an ordered kingdom of the tribes, and the deceiver has no place among them, as John sees him shut in the pit *that he should deceive the nations no more* (Revelation 20:3), until his end in the fire.$n$,$n$And after these things shall Abraham and Isaac and Jacob arise unto life, and I and my brethren shall be chiefs of the tribes 'of Israel': Levi first, I the second, Joseph third, Benjamin fourth, Simeon fifth, Issachar sixth, and so all in order.$n$,false);
INSERT INTO _s463epm VALUES
(416,4869,$n$2 Baruch 6:7 — *I saw him descend into the Holy of Holies, and take from thence the veil, and the holy ark.* The angel who descends and takes the veil in 2 Baruch is the hand from above that tears the veil in Matthew.$n$),
(14123,57962,$n$2 Baruch 29:8 — *the treasury of manna shall again descend from on high.* The manna promised again from on high is the bread of life Yahusha (Jesus) names himself.$n$),
(419,4884,$n$2 Baruch 51:7 — *to whom the law has been now a hope, And understanding an expectation, And wisdom a confidence.* Those for whom the law was a hope are promised sight of the invisible world, and Matthew shows the sleeping saints beginning to rise.$n$),
(103,4427,$n$2 Baruch 70:2 — *the harvest of its evil and good seeds has come.* The harvest of the age, evil and good seeds together, is the harvest Yahusha (Jesus) says is already plenteous.$n$),
(103,4428,$n$2 Baruch 70:2 — *the harvest of its evil and good seeds has come.* The prayer Yahusha (Jesus) teaches in Matthew 9:38 asks for workers for this same harvest.$n$),
(14214,58216,$n$2 Baruch 74:2 — *the consummation of that which is corruptible, And the beginning of that which is not corruptible.* John sees the same passing in Revelation 21:4, where there is no more death because the former things are passed away.$n$),
(105,4431,$n$2 Baruch 78:3 — *all we the twelve tribes are bound by one bond, inasmuch as we are born from one father.* The scattered, shepherdless multitudes Yahusha (Jesus) sees in Matthew 9:36 are this one family born from one father.$n$),
(105,4432,$n$2 Baruch 78:7 — *with much mercy will gather together again those who were dispersed.* The compassion Yahusha (Jesus) shows the scattered sheep in Matthew 9:36 is this promised mercy at work.$n$),
(416,4870,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 21:1 — *the angel opened to me the gates of heaven, and I saw the holy temple.* The gates opened to Levi are the veil torn from the top at the cross.$n$),
(416,4871,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 21:2 — *I have given thee the blessings of the priesthood until I come and sojourn in the midst of Yashar'el (Israel).* The until in Levi's blessing is met when the veil is torn in Matthew 27:51 and the one who sojourns has come.$n$),
(416,4872,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 24:17 — *For by their mouth shall the holy place be guarded.* The faithful dead who rise in Matthew 27:52 are the same covenant line Levi's vision speaks of.$n$),
(414,4861,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 26:2 — *I am clear from your ungodliness and transgression, which ye shall commit in the end of the ages.* Levi's warning of ungodly leaders at the end of the ages stands behind the smitten shepherd and scattered flock of Matthew 26:31.$n$),
(397,4789,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 26:3 — *ye shall deal lawlessly together with Yashar'el (Israel), so He shall not bear with Jerusalem because of your wickedness.* Levi's lawless leaders who hold the door are the ones Yahusha (Jesus) faces in the first woe of Matthew 23:13.$n$),
(414,4862,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 26:3 — *the veil of the temple shall be rent, so as not to cover your shame.* The high priest rends his clothes in Matthew 26:65, and the veil that Levi said would be rent is torn soon after.$n$),
(378,4710,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 29:5 — *Work righteousness, therefore, my children, upon the earth, That ye may have (it) as a treasure in heaven.* Levi's call to work righteousness on the earth and have it as a treasure in heaven is the word Yahusha (Jesus) speaks in Matthew 19:21.$n$),
(397,4790,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 33:11 — *in the seventh week shall come priests, (who are) idolaters, adulterers, lovers of money, proud, lawless.* Levi's seventh-week priests, lawless and proud, are the kind of leaders Yahusha (Jesus) charges in Matthew 23:15.$n$),
(385,4739,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 59:1 — *shall a star arise to you from Jacob in peace, And a man shall arise.* The star out of Jacob from Yahudah's (Judah's) seed is the Son of David the blind men call on.$n$),
(385,4740,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 59:4 — *This Branch of Elohim (God) El Elyon (Most High), And this Fountain giving life unto all.* The Branch from Yahudah's (Judah's) line is the Son of David the two blind men call out to in Matthew 20:30.$n$),
(385,4741,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 59:5 — *the sceptre of my kingdom shine forth; And from your root shall arise a stem.* Two blind men keep crying Son of David against the crowd in Matthew 20:31, naming the stem Yahudah (Judah) was told would rise.$n$),
(386,4742,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 59:5 — *the sceptre of my kingdom shine forth; And from your root shall arise a stem.* The sceptre promised to Yahudah (Judah) comes as the meek King on a colt in Matthew 21:5.$n$),
(386,4743,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 59:6 — *a rod of righteousness to the Gentiles, To judge and to save all that call upon Yahuah (Lord).* Yahudah's (Judah's) rod of righteousness for the Gentiles points to the King coming in Matthew 21:5, whose call goes to the scattered seed.$n$),
(405,4824,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 90:1 — *I saw a vision on the Mount of Olives, on the east of Jerusalem.* Naphtali saw his vision on the same Mount of Olives where the disciples ask about the end in Matthew 24:3.$n$),
(405,4825,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 93:3 — *To save the race of Yashar'el (Israel), And to gather together the righteous from amongst the Gentiles.* The gospel preached to all nations in Matthew 24:14 is the news that the scattered are being gathered.$n$),
(53,4339,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 100:2 — *the spirit of hatred darkened my mind, and stirred up my soul to slay him.* Gad confesses that hatred began as a darkened mind and ended in a plan to kill, which is the very path Yahusha (Jesus) traces back to anger.$n$),
(53,4341,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 100:3 — *if a man sin against thee, speak peaceably to him, and in thy soul hold not guile.* Gad tells his sons to answer a brother's wrong with peace and forgiveness, which is the same heart Yahusha (Jesus) asks for toward an enemy.$n$),
(374,4695,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 100:3 — *Love ye one another from the heart.* Gad's call to love from the heart and forgive the repentant brother stands behind the warning that closes Yahusha's (Jesus's) teaching on forgiveness.$n$),
(399,4798,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 105:1 — *wear two faces like unto them, of goodness and of wickedness.* Asher charges his sons not to wear two faces, the same split between outside and inside that Yahusha (Jesus) calls hypocrisy.$n$),
(399,4799,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 108:2 — *they that are double-faced are guilty of a twofold sin.* Asher says the double-faced carry a twofold sin, and Yahusha (Jesus) paints the same figure as a whited tomb.$n$),
(405,4826,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 109:3 — *coming Himself [as man, with men eating and drinking], and breaking the head of the dragon in the water.* Asher says the Most High will come to the earth Himself in the person of man, and Matthew shows that coming with the tribes watching.$n$),
(405,4827,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 109:7 — *Yahuah (Lord) will gather you together in faith through His tender mercy.* Asher promises that Yahuah (the Lord) will gather the scattered sons for the sake of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, and Matthew describes the elect being gathered from the four winds.$n$),
(380,4720,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 129:2 — *There were twelve harts feeding: and the nine were (first) dispersed over all the earth.* Joseph's vision of twelve harts dispersed over the earth is the scattering that Yahusha (Jesus) assumes when He speaks of judging the twelve tribes.$n$),
(414,4863,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 133:8 — *a blameless one shall be delivered up for lawless men, and a sinless shall die for ungodly men.* Jacob's word that a sinless one will die for ungodly men in the blood of the covenant is the death Yahusha (Jesus) names at the table.$n$),
(14853,60366,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 133:6 — *besought our father 'that he would pray for his brethren', that 'the Lord' would not impute to them as sin.* Joseph asked his father to pray for the brothers who wronged him, which is the love of enemies Yahusha (Jesus) later commands.$n$),
(14854,60364,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 133:8 — *a blameless one shall be delivered up for lawless men, and a sinless shall die for ungodly men.* Jacob foretells a sinless one dying for ungodly men, and Peter names the Messiah (Christ) as the just one who suffered for the unjust.$n$),
(671,8023,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 134:5 — *him that hath the grace of a good spirit he loveth as his own soul.* Benjamin teaches loving a brother as one's own soul, the measure that John 15:13 carries to laying down one's life.$n$),
(384,4737,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 139:5 — *I know how lowly He shall be upon earth, and how glorious in heaven.* Benjamin foresees the one who will be lowly on earth and glorious in heaven, and Yahusha (Jesus) says the Son of Adam came to serve and give His life.$n$),
(425,4908,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 139:5 — *He shall ascend from Hades and shall pass from earth into heaven.* Benjamin foresees the ascent from Hades into heaven, and Yahusha (Jesus) states the power given Him in heaven and in earth.$n$),
(425,4909,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 140:5 — *Keep the commandments of Elohim (God), until Yahuah (Lord) shall reveal His salvation to all Gentiles.* Benjamin's sons are left the commandments to keep while they wait for the salvation to be revealed to all the Gentiles, and Yahusha (Jesus) sends His own out to every nation.$n$),
(425,4910,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 140:7 — *Then shall we also rise, each one over our tribe, worshipping the King of heaven.* Benjamin sees the patriarchs rising each over his tribe to worship the King, and Yahusha (Jesus) after rising calls His own brethren.$n$),
(425,4911,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 140:8 — *Yahuah (Lord) shall judge Yashar'el (Israel) first, for their unrighteousness.* Benjamin says Yahuah (the Lord) will judge Yashar'el (Israel) first, and Yahusha (Jesus) holds the power in heaven and in earth to do it.$n$),
(12373,51071,$n$Revelation 14:13 — *Blessed are the dead which die in Yahusha (Lord) from henceforth: Yea, saith the Spirit, that they may rest from their labours; and their works do follow them.* The flowers that are the merits of the righteous, carried up to God, are the works John says follow the saints who die in the Lord.$n$),
(12378,51087,$n$Revelation 14:13 — *Blessed are the dead which die in Yahusha (Lord) from henceforth: Yea, saith the Spirit, that they may rest from their labours; and their works do follow them.* The good works gathered into the full baskets are the works that follow the righteous and are rewarded.$n$),
(13384,55277,$n$2 Peter 3:8 — *But, beloved, be not ignorant of this one thing, that one day is with Yahuah (Lord) as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day.* The "seventh thousand" and the eighth thousand of 2 Enoch 33:1 rest on the apostle's measure of a day as a thousand years before the Lord.$n$),
(14085,57887,$n$2 Peter 3:9 — *Yahuah (Lord) is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness; but is longsuffering to us-ward* — the 'long-suffering' that holds the wrath by reins, named by the apostle.$n$),
(14092,57901,$n$Revelation 14:13 — *Blessed are the dead which die in Yahusha (Lord) from henceforth: Yea, saith the Spirit, that they may rest from their labours; and their works do follow them.* — the righteous departing without fear, their works 'preserved in treasuries.'$n$),
(14114,57950,$n$Revelation 6:10 — *And they cried with a loud voice, saying, How long, O Yahuah (Lord), holy and true, dost thou not judge and avenge our blood on them that dwell on the earth?* Baruch's question whether the tribulation will continue many years is the same "how long" the martyred souls cry under the altar.$n$),
(14125,57979,$n$1 Thessalonians 4:16 — *For Yahusha (Lord) himself shall descend from heaven with a shout, with the voice of the archangel, and with the trump of Elohim (God): and the dead in Messiah (Christ) shall rise first:* That those asleep in hope of Him rise again at His glorious return is Paul's word that at the descent from heaven the dead in Messiah rise first.$n$),
(14138,58009,$n$2 Thessalonians 2:8 — *whom Yahusha (Lord) shall consume with the spirit of his mouth, and shall destroy with the brightness of his coming:* — the last wicked one burned away before the reign that grows in peace.$n$),
(14143,58029,$n$2 Thess 2:8 — *And then shall that Wicked be revealed, whom Yahusha (Lord) shall consume with the spirit of his mouth, and shall destroy with the brightness of his coming:* — the lawless one slain by the Messiah's word, the same convicting-and-slaying Baruch describes.$n$),
(14156,58066,$n$Rom 4:17 — *even Elohim (God), who quickeneth the dead, and calleth those things which be not as though they were.* — with a word He quickens that which was not.$n$),
(14165,58080,$n$Rom 2:13 — *For not the hearers of the law are just before Elohim (God), but the doers of the law shall be justified.* — the lost stopped their ears against the law and so were condemned.$n$),
(14184,58136,$n$1 Chr 22:9 — *who shall be a man of rest; and I will give him rest from all his enemies round about: for his name shall be Solomon, and I will give peace and quietness unto Yashar'el (Israel) in his days.* — Solomon, the man of rest, in whose days the land was beloved and glorified, as Baruch tells.$n$),
(14242,58270,$n$2 Cor 6:2 — *behold, now is the accepted time; behold, now is the day of salvation.* — the open day of repentance Baruch says will not return once the age is past, so turn now.$n$),
(14794,60179,$n$Ezek 37:27 — *My tabernacle also shall be with them: yea, I will be their Elohim (God), and they shall be my people.* The Lord in the midst of His restored city, exactly as Dan promises Jerusalem.$n$),
(14793,60185,$n$Rev 21:2 — *And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from Elohim (God) out of heaven*. The very New Jerusalem in which Dan says the righteous shall rejoice.$n$),
(14792,60186,$n$Rev 20:6 — *but they shall be priests of Elohim (God) and of Messiah (Christ), and shall reign with him a thousand years.* The saints whose captivity is taken from Beliar, reigning in the peace Dan promises them.$n$),
(14791,60190,$n$Num 24:17 — *there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel)*. Balaam's Sceptre, the king from Judah whom Dan joins with Levi as the salvation of the Lord.$n$),
(14796,60192,$n$Deut 30:4 — *from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee, and from thence will he fetch thee:* The Lord's name in every place of Israel and among the Gentiles — the gathering of the scattered Dan foresees.$n$),
(14796,60194,$n$Deut 30:2 — *And shalt return unto Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), and shalt obey his voice according to all that I command thee this day, thou and thy children, with all thine heart*. The day of Israel's repentance on which Dan says the enemy's kingdom ends.$n$),
(14795,60196,$n$1 Tim 2:5 — *For there is one Elohim (God), and one mediator between Elohim (God) and men, the man HaMashiach Yahusha (Christ Jesus);* The single mediator Dan tells his sons to draw near to — the appointed Anointed, not a co-equal, but the man who stands between God and Israel.$n$),
(14838,60319,$n$2 Timothy 2:22 — *Flee also youthful lusts: but follow righteousness, faith, charity, peace, with them that call on Yahusha (Lord) out of a pure heart.* Joseph's weeping, praying, and fasting is exactly the fleeing of youthful lust by calling on the Lord that Paul charges Timothy.$n$),
(14842,60332,$n$2 Timothy 2:22 — *Flee also youthful lusts: but follow righteousness, faith, charity, peace, with them that call on Yahusha (Lord) out of a pure heart.* That God loves him "who in a den of darkness combines fasting with chastity" over the man of luxury and licence is Paul's same preference of righteousness over youthful lust.$n$),
(14851,60361,$n$Gen 37:28 — *and sold Joseph to the Ishmeelites for twenty pieces of silver: and they brought Joseph into Egypt.* — the very sale Joseph names, "they gave me to the Ishmaelites."$n$),
(14863,60397,$n$Deut 21:23 — *for he that is hanged is accursed of Elohim (God)* — the Torah's word on the one hanged on a tree, the curse the lifted-up Lord bears.$n$),
(14710,59968,$n$2 Enoch 3:1 — *bore him up on to the first heaven and placed him on the clouds ... and showed me a very great Sea, greater than the earthly sea.* Enoch's ascent to the first heaven and its great sea is the same first heaven and "great sea hanging" Levi enters.$n$),
(673,8018,$n$Gad, Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 99:1 — *Hatred ... mateth with lying, speaking against the truth ... causeth the light to be darkness ... it filleth the heart with evils and devilish poison.* Hatred is the engine that turns the truth over and calls the Light darkness; John 15:18's *If the world hate you, ye know that it hated me before it hated you* names the same poison turned against the Formed one and his own.$n$),
(13431,55409,$n$Genesis 9:6 — *Whoso sheddeth man's blood, by man shall his blood be shed: for in the image of Elohim (God) made he man.* "He who works the killing of a man’s soul, kills his own soul" is the word given Noah — the shedder of man's blood has his own blood shed, for man bears Elohim's image.$n$),
(13437,55426,$n$Genesis 5:24 — *And Enoch walked with Elohim (God): and he was not; for Elohim (God) took him.* The Enoch the people bless as one Yahuah "chose you, rather than all men on earth" in 2 Enoch 64:5 is the man Moses records as walking with Elohim and being taken — honored, not deified.$n$),
(13438,55434,$n$Revelation 22:5 — *And there shall be no night there; and they need no candle, neither light of the sun; for Yahuah Elohim (the Lord God) giveth them light: and they shall reign for ever and ever.* The "nor night, nor darkness, but great light" of 2 Enoch 65:6 is John's city where there is no night and Yahuah Himself is the light.$n$),
(13441,55437,$n$Psalms 139:8 — *If I ascend up into heaven, thou art there: if I make my bed in hell, behold, thou art there.* The "If you look to heaven, Yahuah Shammah (the Lord is there)... and all the under-earth, Yahuah Shammah (the Lord is there)" of 2 Enoch 66:5 is David's confession that Yahuah fills heaven and the depth alike.$n$),
(14085,57889,$n$Habakkuk 2:3 — *For the vision is yet for an appointed time, but at the end it shall speak, and not lie: though it tarry, wait for it; because it will surely come* — the wrath that 'in its own season shall the (divine) wrath awake' the appointed delay Baruch describes.$n$),
(14090,57906,$n$Romans 11:33 — *O the depth of the riches both of the wisdom and knowledge of Elohim (God)! how unsearchable are his judgments, and his ways past finding out!* — Baruch's 'who, O Yahuah (LORD), my Lord, will comprehend Thy judgement' in the apostle's very words.$n$),
(14698,59929,$n$Gen 37:27 — *Come, and let us sell him to the Ishmeelites, and let not our hand be upon him; for he is our brother and our flesh. And his brethren were content.* — Judah's counsel that Simeon recalls, "Yahudah (Judah) my brother sold him to the Ishmaelites."$n$),
(14700,59935,$n$Prov 14:27 — *The fear of Yahuah (LORD) is a fountain of life, to depart from the snares of death.* — the very deliverance Simeon found: "deliverance from envy cometh by the fear of Elohim (God)."$n$),
(14699,59936,$n$James 3:16 — *For where envying and strife is, there is confusion and every evil work.* — envy's fruit, the same root Simeon names that "suffereth him 'neither to eat nor to drink', nor to do any good thing."$n$),
(14704,59944,$n$Zech 6:13 — *and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.* — the division "in Levi and Yahudah (Judah)," priest and king at peace, that Simeon names.$n$),
(14703,59946,$n$Gen 6:11 — *The earth also was corrupt before Elohim (God), and the earth was filled with violence.* — fornication "mother of all evils," filling the earth with corruption as in Noah's day.$n$),
(14703,59947,$n$Gen 6:2 — *That the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair; and they took them wives of all which they chose.* — the fornication of the Watchers that "bringing near to Beliar," the root Enoch expounds.$n$),
(14705,59952,$n$Gen 9:26 — *Blessed be Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) of Shem; and Canaan shall be his servant.* — "the Mighty One of Yashar'el (Israel) shall glorify Shem" and Canaan perish, Noah's blessing fulfilled.$n$),
(14707,59956,$n$Heb 7:25 — *Wherefore he is able also to save them to the uttermost that come unto Elohim (God) by him, seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.* — "He shall save all [the Gentiles and] the race of Yashar'el (Israel)," the salvation arising from the two tribes.$n$),
(14712,59974,$n$Isaiah 6:3 — *Holy, holy, holy, is Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts): the whole earth is full of his glory.* The thrones and dominions that 'always they offer praise to Elohim (God)' echo the seraphim's unceasing cry.$n$),
(14714,59977,$n$Isaiah 9:2 — *The people that walked in darkness have seen a great light.* Levi lighting 'The light of knowledge shalt thou light up in Jacob' and shining 'as the sun shalt thou be to all the seed of Yashar'el (Israel)' is the great light upon the people.$n$),
(14715,59982,$n$Malachi 3:1 — *Yahuah (Lord), whom ye seek, shall suddenly come to his temple.* 'until I come and sojourn in the midst of Yashar'el (Israel)' is the Lord's promised coming to His temple.$n$),
(14719,59986,$n$Hebrews 7:12 — *For the priesthood being changed, there is made of necessity a change also of the law.* That Levi's seed is divided 'for a sign of the glory of Yahuah (Lord) who is to come' answers to the changed priesthood Hebrews names.$n$),
(14724,60002,$n$Matthew 6:20 — *But lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust doth corrupt.* 'Work righteousness... That ye may have (it) as a treasure in heaven' is the treasure laid up above.$n$),
(14724,60003,$n$Deuteronomy 6:5 — *And thou shalt love Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) with all thine heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy might.* 'Fear Yahuah Elohaychem (the Lord your God) with your whole heart' is the Shema's command of whole-hearted love.$n$),
(14725,60006,$n$Malachi 2:7 — *the priest's lips should keep knowledge, and they should seek the law at his mouth: for he is the messenger of Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts).* The office the priests forsake when 'puffed up because of your priesthood' is the lips that should keep knowledge.$n$),
(14732,60017,$n$Genesis 3:24 — *he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.* 'he shall open the gates of paradise, And shall remove the threatening sword against Adam' undoes the flaming sword that barred Eden.$n$),
(14729,60026,$n$Psalm 110:4 — *Yahuah (LORD) hath sworn, and will not repent, Thou art a priest for ever after the order of Melek Tsadiq (Melchizedek).* The new priest Yahuah (the Lord) raises up, to whom all his words are revealed and who judges the earth for a multitude of days, is the priest Yahuah (the LORD) swore in after the order of Melek Tsadiq (Melchizedek) — a priesthood not from Levi's line and not for a season.$n$),
(14734,60027,$n$Deuteronomy 30:19 — *I call heaven and earth to record this day against you... therefore choose life.* 'Yahuah (Lord) is witness, and His angels are witnesses, and ye are witnesses' is Moses' calling of heaven and earth to record the choice of life.$n$),
(14734,60028,$n$Deuteronomy 30:15 — *See, I have set before thee this day life and good, and death and evil.* 'choose, therefore, for yourselves either the light or the darkness, either the law of Yahuah (Lord) or the works of Beliar' is the life-and-death Moses set before Israel.$n$),
(14739,60042,$n$Genesis 38:26 — *And Yahudah (Judah) acknowledged them, and said, She hath been more righteous than I; because that I gave her not to Shelah my son. And he knew her again no more.* Judah's "she privily sent my pledges, and put me to shame" is the same confession Moses sets down.$n$),
(14747,60057,$n$Genesis 49:10 — *The sceptre shall not depart from Yahudah (Judah), nor a lawgiver from between his feet, until Shiloh come; and unto him shall the gathering of the people be.* The kingdom "from me shall the kingdom be established" is the scepter Jacob fixed on Judah.$n$),
(14753,60075,$n$Isaiah 45:17 — *But Yashar'el (Israel) shall be saved in Yahuah (LORD) with an everlasting salvation: ye shall not be ashamed nor confounded world without end.* The coming "salvation of Yashar'el (Israel)" and rest in peace is Isaiah's everlasting salvation.$n$),
(14753,60076,$n$Genesis 49:10 — *The sceptre shall not depart from Yahudah (Judah), nor a lawgiver from between his feet, until Shiloh come; and unto him shall the gathering of the people be.* The kingdom held "Until the salvation of Yashar'el (Israel) shall come" is the scepter held until Shiloh comes.$n$),
(14757,60085,$n$Isaiah 11:1 — *And there shall come forth a rod out of the stem of Jesse, and a Branch shall grow out of his roots.* "This Branch of Elohim (God) El Elyon (Most High)" is Isaiah's Branch grown from the roots of Jesse.$n$),
(14755,60091,$n$Numbers 24:17 — *...there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Yashar'el (Israel), and shall smite the corners of Moab, and destroy all the children of Sheth.* Judah's "shall a star arise to you from Jacob" is Balaam's very oracle of the Star and Sceptre.$n$),
(14768,60113,$n$Genesis 49:10 — *The sceptre shall not depart from Yahudah (Judah), nor a lawgiver from between his feet, until Shiloh come; and unto him shall the gathering of the people be.* "to Yahudah (Judah) the kingdom" is Jacob's own dying word over Judah's sceptre.$n$),
(14766,60116,$n$Matthew 22:40 — *On these two commandments hang all the law and the prophets.* Issachar's "Keep, therefore, my children, the law of Elohim (God)" reduced to love of God and neighbour is the very hinge the Master names.$n$),
(14781,60154,$n$Matthew 5:7 — *Blessed are the merciful: for they shall obtain mercy.* "Have, therefore, yourselves also, my children, compassion... that Yahuah (Lord) also may have compassion and mercy upon you" is the Beatitude almost word for word.$n$),
(14783,60162,$n$Ezekiel 37:22 — *And I will make them one nation in the land upon the mountains of Yashar'el (Israel); and one king shall be king to them all: and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all.* Zebulun's "Ye shall be divided in Yashar'el (Israel), And ye shall follow two kings" is the very division of the two kingdoms Ezekiel says shall at last be made one.$n$),
(14799,60202,$n$Genesis 1:31 — *And Elohim (God) saw every thing that he had made, and, behold, it was very good. And the evening and the morning were the sixth day.* — "Elohim (God) made all things good in their order" echoes the verdict over the whole creation, that it was very good.$n$),
(14800,60216,$n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple.* — "change not the law of Elohim (God)" rests on the law that is perfect, the same psalm that begins with the ordered heavens.$n$),
(14802,60221,$n$Deuteronomy 30:3 — *That then Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) will turn thy captivity, and have compassion upon thee, and will return and gather thee from all the nations, whither Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) hath scattered thee.* — "ye shall return and acknowledge Yahuah Elohaychem (the Lord your God); and He shall bring you back into your own land, according to His abundant mercy" is the turning of the captivity and the gathering Moses promised.$n$),
(14808,60233,$n$Psalm 19:7 — *The law of Yahuah (LORD) is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah (LORD) is sure, making wise the simple.* — "Be ye therefore wise in Elohim (God)... understanding the order of His commandments" rests on the law that is perfect and makes the simple wise.$n$),
(14807,60235,$n$John 1:14 — *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.* — "Elohim (God) shall appear, dwelling among men on earth" is fulfilled when the Word was made flesh and dwelt among us — the only begotten whom the Father sent, the Formed one walking among men.$n$),
(14807,60239,$n$Zechariah 2:10 — *Sing and rejoice, O daughter of Zion: for, lo, I come, and I will dwell in the midst of thee, saith Yahuah (LORD).* — "shall Elohim (God) appear [dwelling among men] on earth" is the LORD's own promise to come and dwell in the midst of Zion.$n$),
(14821,60274,$n$Psalms 37:1 — *Fret not thyself because of evildoers, neither be thou envious against the workers of iniquity.* Gad's 'do not be vexed... be not envious' when another prospers is David's own counsel against envy.$n$),
(14826,60288,$n$Leviticus 11:6 — *And the hare, because he cheweth the cud, but divideth not the hoof; he is unclean unto you.* Asher's "half clean, but in very deed are unclean" hare is the very creature Moses names: it answers one mark of cleanness and fails the other, like the double-faced man.$n$),
(14833,60307,$n$Genesis 19:24 — *Then Yahuah (LORD) rained upon Sodom and upon Gomorrah brimstone and fire from Yahuah (LORD) out of heaven;* Asher's warning, "Become not, my children, as Sodom, which knew not the angels of Yahuah (Lord), and perished for ever," recalls the city that rejected the two angels and was destroyed.$n$),
(14836,60310,$n$Genesis 39:2 — *And Yahuah (LORD) was with Joseph, and he was a prosperous man; and he was in the house of his master the Egyptian.* The refrain of the whole testament — "Yahuah (Lord) loved me... the Elohim (God) of my fathers guarded me" — is Moses' own refrain over Joseph.$n$),
(14838,60321,$n$Genesis 39:10 — *And it came to pass, as she spake to Joseph day by day, that he hearkened not unto her, to lie by her, or to be with her.* The woman's repeated threatening "How often did the Egyptian woman threaten me with death!... and then call me back and threaten me" is Moses' "day by day."$n$),
(14845,60338,$n$Genesis 45:1 — *Then Joseph could not refrain himself before all them that stood by him; and he cried, Cause every man to go out from me.* That Joseph here "desired greatly to weep, but I restrained myself" is the same overflowing heart Moses records breaking forth before his brethren.$n$),
(14846,60339,$n$Leviticus 19:18 — *Thou shalt not avenge, nor bear any grudge against the children of thy people, but thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am Yahuah (LORD).* "love one another, and with long-suffering hide 'ye one another's faults'" is the royal commandment in plain words.$n$),
(14869,60421,$n$Deut 30:4 — *from thence will Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) gather thee, and from thence will he fetch thee.* — the gathering of "all Yashar'el (Israel) shall be gathered unto Yahuah (Lord)" Benjamin foresees.$n$),
(53,4340,$n$Reuben, Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 3:1 — *an eighth spirit of sleep, with which is brought about the trance of nature and the image of death.* Reuben lists the spirits that work in a man through his nature and his senses, the first of them being fornication — *First, the spirit of fornication is seated in the nature and in the senses* (Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 3:3) — and Yahusha (Jesus) puts the sin in the same place when he says that whoever looks on a woman to lust after her *hath committed adultery with her already in his heart* (Matthew 5:28).$n$),
(58,4354,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 64:7 — *Jacob, my father, knew that Elohim (God) aided my singleness.* Issachar's single heart is an open hand toward the poor, and Yahusha (Jesus) says, *if therefore thine eye be single, thy whole body shall be full of light* (Matthew 6:22).$n$),
(39,4291,$n$Testaments of the Twelve Patriarchs 18:6 — *behold the heavens were opened, and an angel of Elohim (God) said to me, Levi, enter.* The heavens open over Levi at his priestly investiture; they open again over Yahusha (Jesus) at the Jordan (Matthew 3:16), the Messiah's own investiture.$n$);
INSERT INTO _s463eps VALUES
(12344,$n$Baruch voices the captive's deepest wound — not the loss of stone, but the taunt that Yahuah has failed: *thou didst deliver us to nations such as these, so that they reproach us and say, Where is their Elohim (God)?* (3 Baruch 1:3). This is the cry the Psalms already carry: *Wherefore should the heathen say, Where is their Elohim (God)? let him be known among the heathen in our sight by the revenging of the blood of thy servants* (Psalms 79:10), and *My tears have been my meat day and night, while they continually say unto me, Where is thy Elohim (God)?* (Psalms 42:3). Jeremiah names the desolation that gives the taunt its sting: *Then will I cause to cease from the cities of Yahudah (Judah), and from the streets of Jerusalem, the voice of mirth, and the voice of gladness... for the land shall be desolate* (Jeremiah 7:34). Baruch's question is old; the answer the angel brings — that the prayer was heard — is older still.$n$,$n$Baruch voices the captive's deepest wound — not the loss of stone, but the taunt that Yahuah has failed: *didst deliver us to nations such as these, so that they reproach us and say, Where is their Elohim (God)?* (3 Baruch 1:3). This is the cry the Psalms already carry: *Wherefore should the heathen say, Where is their Elohim (God)? let him be known among the heathen in our sight by the revenging of the blood of thy servants* (Psalm 79:10), and *My tears have been my meat day and night, while they continually say unto me, Where is thy Elohim (God)?* (Psalm 42:3). Jeremiah names the desolation that gives the taunt its sting: *Then will I cause to cease from the cities of Yahudah (Judah), and from the streets of Jerusalem, the voice of mirth, and the voice of gladness... for the land shall be desolate* (Jeremiah 7:34). Baruch's question is old; the answer the angel brings — that the prayer was heard — is older still.$n$),
(12349,$n$The builders' presumption reaches its height: *they took a gimlet, and sought to pierce the heaven, saying, Let us see whether the heaven is made of clay, or of brass, or of iron* (3 Baruch 3:7); and the judgment falls: *When Elohim (God) saw this He did not permit them, but smote them with blindness and confusion of speech* (3 Baruch 3:8). This is Genesis exactly — the LORD coming down to the tower that reached for heaven: *And Yahuah (LORD) said, Behold, the people is one, and they have all one language; and this they begin to do: and now nothing will be restrained from them, which they have imagined to do* (Genesis 11:6), *Go to, let us go down, and there confound their language, that they may not understand one another's speech* (Genesis 11:7). Jubilees names the same confounding: *And He confounded their language, and they no longer understood one another's speech, and they ceased then to build the city and the tower* (Jubilees 10:24). The presumption that would pierce heaven ends in confusion of tongues. It ain't new.$n$,$n$The builders' presumption reaches its height: *took a gimlet, and sought to pierce the heaven, saying, Let us see (whether) the heaven is made of clay, or of brass, or of iron* (3 Baruch 3:7); and the judgment falls: *When Elohim (God) saw this He did not permit them, but smote them with blindness and confusion of speech* (3 Baruch 3:8). This is Genesis exactly — Yahuah coming down to the tower that reached for heaven: *And Yahuah (LORD) said, Behold, the people is one, and they have all one language; and this they begin to do: and now nothing will be restrained from them, which they have imagined to do* (Genesis 11:6), *Go to, let us go down, and there confound their language, that they may not understand one another's speech* (Genesis 11:7). Jubilees names the same confounding: *And He confounded their language, and they no longer understood one another's speech, and they ceased then to build the city and the tower* (Jubilees 10:24). The presumption that would pierce heaven ends in confusion of tongues. It ain't new.$n$),
(13337,$n$Before he ascends, Enoch charges his sons with the first commandment's substance: *turn not from Elohim (God) before the face of the vain, who made not Heaven and earth, for these shall perish and those who worship them, and may Yahuah (Lord) make confident your hearts in the fear of him* (2 Enoch 2:1). The dividing line he draws — the Maker against the made — is Moses' and the prophets' own line. Moses set it as the day's whole knowledge: *Know therefore this day, and consider it in thine heart, that Yahuah (LORD) he is Elohim (God) in heaven above, and upon the earth beneath: there is none else* (Deuteronomy 4:39). Jeremiah names the doom of the false gods in nearly the same breath as Enoch: *The gods that have not made the heavens and the earth, even they shall perish from the earth, and from under these heavens* (Jeremiah 10:11). And Isaiah exposes the vanity Enoch warns against: *they worship the work of their own hands, that which their own fingers have made* (Isaiah 2:8). It ain't new — the patriarch's parting word is the Shema's own fence.$n$,$n$Before he ascends, Enoch charges his sons to hold to the first commandment: *turn not from Elohim (God) before the face of the vain, who made not Heaven and earth, for these shall perish and those who worship them, and may Yahuah (Lord) make confident your hearts in the fear of him* (2 Enoch 2:1). The dividing line he draws — the Maker against the made — is Moses' and the prophets' own line. Moses set it as the day's whole knowledge: *Know therefore this day, and consider it in thine heart, that Yahuah (LORD) he is Elohim (God) in heaven above, and upon the earth beneath: there is none else* (Deuteronomy 4:39). Jeremiah names the doom of the false gods in nearly the same breath as Enoch: *The gods that have not made the heavens and the earth, even they shall perish from the earth, and from under these heavens* (Jeremiah 10:11). And Isaiah exposes the vanity Enoch warns against: *they worship the work of their own hands, that which their own fingers have made* (Isaiah 2:8). It ain't new — the patriarch's parting word is the Shema's own fence.$n$),
(13366,$n$At the Lord's word *the archistratege Michael* takes Enoch *out of his earthly garments, and anoint[s] him with... sweet ointment, and put[s] him into the garments of My glory* (2 Enoch 22:8), and the seer testifies *I looked at myself, and I was like one of his glorious ones* (2 Enoch 22:9). This is no deifying of a man — it is the change scripture promises every servant who stands before the glory. Moses came down with a shining face after speaking with Yahuah (Exodus 34:29); Joshua the priest was stripped and re-robed before the angel — *Take away the filthy garments from him... I will clothe thee with change of raiment* (Zechariah 3:4); and the redeemed are seen *clothed with white robes* before the throne (Revelation 7:9). The apostle names the very transformation: *we all, with open face beholding... the glory of Yahuah (Lord), are changed into the same image from glory to glory* (2 Corinthians 3:18), and He *shall change our vile body, that it may be fashioned like unto his glorious body* (Philippians 3:21). It ain't new — Enoch re-robed in glory is the honored seer transfigured as Moses, Joshua, and every saint shall be.$n$,$n$Yahuah (Lord) says to Michael, *Go and take Enoch from out of his earthly garments, and anoint him with my sweet ointment, and put him into the garments of My glory* (2 Enoch 22:8), and the seer testifies *I looked at myself, and I was like one of his glorious ones* (2 Enoch 22:9). This is no deifying of a man — it is the change scripture promises every servant who stands before the glory. Moses came down with a shining face after speaking with Yahuah (Exodus 34:29); Joshua the priest was stripped and re-robed before the angel — *Take away the filthy garments from him... I will clothe thee with change of raiment* (Zechariah 3:4); and the redeemed are seen *clothed with white robes* before the throne (Revelation 7:9). The apostle names the very transformation: *we all, with open face beholding... the glory of Yahuah (Lord), are changed into the same image from glory to glory* (2 Corinthians 3:18), and He *shall change our vile body, that it may be fashioned like unto his glorious body* (Philippians 3:21). It ain't new — Enoch re-robed in glory is the honored seer transfigured as Moses, Joshua, and every saint shall be.$n$),
(13385,$n$The Lord seals the secrets of creation by naming Himself: *I am self-eternal, not made with hands, and without change. My thought is my counsellor... there is no counsellor nor inheritor to my creations* (2 Enoch 33:3-4), and the books are given that men *will know me for the creator of all things, and will understand how there is no other Elohim (God) but me* (2 Enoch 33:9). This is the bare confession of Moses and the prophets: *Know therefore this day, and consider it in thine heart, that Yahuah (LORD) he is Elohim (God) in heaven above, and upon the earth beneath: there is none else* (Deuteronomy 4:39); *thus saith Yahuah (LORD) that created the heavens... I am Yahuah (LORD); and there is none else* (Isaiah 45:18). And the worlds were framed by His word alone: *Through faith we understand that the worlds were framed by the word of Elohim (God), so that things which are seen were not made of things which do appear* (Hebrews 11:3). It ain't new — "no other Elohim but me" is the Shema's own ground, the Creator confessing Himself as Moses, Isaiah, and the apostles confess Him.$n$,$n$Yahuah (Lord) seals the secrets of creation by naming Himself: *I am self-eternal, not made with hands, and without change. My thought is my counsellor* (2 Enoch 33:3–4), and the books are given that men *will know me for the creator of all things, and will understand how there is no other Elohim (God) but me* (2 Enoch 33:9). This is the bare confession of Moses and the prophets: *Know therefore this day, and consider it in thine heart, that Yahuah (LORD) he is Elohim (God) in heaven above, and upon the earth beneath: there is none else* (Deuteronomy 4:39); *thus saith Yahuah (LORD) that created the heavens... I am Yahuah (LORD); and there is none else* (Isaiah 45:18). And the worlds were framed by His word alone: *Through faith we understand that the worlds were framed by the word of Elohim (God), so that things which are seen were not made of things which do appear* (Hebrews 11:3). It ain't new — "no other Elohim (God) but me" is the Shema's own ground, the Creator confessing Himself as Moses, Isaiah, and the apostles confess Him.$n$),
(14119,$n$Baruch asks whether the woes fall on one region or all the world: *Is it in one place or in one of the parts of the earth that those things are come to pass, or will the whole earth experience them?* (2 Baruch 28:7). The answer the prophets give is that the day of Yahuah is upon all the earth — *the indignation of Yahuah is upon all nations* (Isaiah 34:2) — and the Messiah's gospel of the end is preached *in all the world for a witness unto all nations; and then shall the end come* (Matthew 24:14). It ain't new — the consummation is appointed for the whole earth, not one corner.$n$,$n$Baruch asks whether the woes fall on one region or all the world: *Is it in one place or in one of the parts of the earth that those things are come to pass, or will the whole earth experience (them)?* (2 Baruch 28:7). The answer the prophets give is that the day of Yahuah is upon all the earth — *the indignation of Yahuah is upon all nations* (Isaiah 34:2) — and the Messiah's gospel of the kingdom is preached *in all the world for a witness unto all nations; and then shall the end come* (Matthew 24:14). It ain't new — the consummation is appointed for the whole earth, not one corner.$n$),
(14123,$n$At the consummation the bread of heaven returns for the saved: *the treasury of manna shall again descend from on high, and they will eat of it in those years* (2 Baruch 29:8). Moses recorded the first rain of it, *I will rain bread from heaven for you* (Exodus 16:4) — and the Messiah declared Himself its true and final substance, *our fathers did eat manna in the desert... my Father giveth you the true bread from heaven* (John 6:31-32), *I am the bread of life: he that cometh to me shall never hunger* (John 6:35). It ain't new — the manna that comes down again is Moses' bread from heaven, and the Messiah is the true bread it foreshadowed.$n$,$n$At the consummation the bread of heaven returns for the saved: *the treasury of manna shall again descend from on high, and they will eat of it in those years* (2 Baruch 29:8). Moses recorded the first rain of it, *I will rain bread from heaven for you* (Exodus 16:4) — and the Messiah declared Himself the true bread of which it spoke, *our fathers did eat manna in the desert... my Father giveth you the true bread from heaven* (John 6:31-32), *I am the bread of life: he that cometh to me shall never hunger* (John 6:35). It ain't new — the manna that comes down again is Moses' bread from heaven, and the Messiah is the true bread it foreshadowed.$n$),
(14811,$n$Gad confesses that he often wished to kill Joseph, hating him from the heart and yet the more for his dreams. Genesis records the dreams that drew the brethren's hatred, and the apostle John names what such hatred truly is — a murderer's heart. It ain't new — Gad's confession is the very murder-in-the-heart John warns against.$n$,$n$Gad confesses that he often wished to kill Joseph, hating him from the heart and yet the more for his dreams. Genesis records the dreams that drew the brethren's hatred — *And his brethren said to him, Shalt thou indeed reign over us? or shalt thou indeed have dominion over us? And they hated him yet the more for his dreams, and for his words* (Genesis 37:8) — and the apostle John names what such hatred truly is — *Whosoever hateth his brother is a murderer: and ye know that no murderer hath eternal life abiding in him* (1 John 3:15). It ain't new — Gad's confession is the very murder in the heart that John warns against.$n$),
(14854,$n$Jacob's blessing over Joseph reaches past Joseph: a prophecy that a blameless one shall be delivered up for lawless men, a sinless die for the ungodly, for the salvation of the Gentiles and of Israel, to destroy Beliar. The good man who was sold and forgave is the type; the Branch from Levi and Judah is the substance — the Anointed delivered up, raised, who brings salvation to the nations. It ain't new — Isaiah's lamb led to the slaughter is the root of which Joseph is the shadow.$n$,$n$Jacob's blessing over Joseph reaches past Joseph: a prophecy that a blameless one shall be delivered up for lawless men, a sinless one die for the ungodly, for the salvation of the Gentiles and of Yashar'el (Israel), to destroy Beliar. Joseph is the good man who was sold and forgave, and the prophecy points beyond him to the Branch from Levi and Yahudah (Judah), the Anointed delivered up and raised. It ain't new — *He was oppressed, and he was afflicted, yet he opened not his mouth: he is brought as a lamb to the slaughter, and as a sheep before her shearers is dumb, so he openeth not his mouth* (Isaiah 53:7) — the lamb led to the slaughter in Isaiah is the one Joseph's life points to.$n$),
(12362,$n$*Because it beholds the lawlessness and unrighteousness of men, namely fornications, adulteries, thefts, extortions, idolatries, drunkenness, murders, strife, jealousies, evil-speakings, murmurings, whisperings, divinations, and such like, which are not well-pleasing to Elohim.* It ain't new. The catalog of sins under which the very light is grieved is the indictment of every age. From the flood-world on, *Elohim saw that the wickedness of man was great in the earth, and that every imagination of the thoughts of his heart was only evil continually* (Genesis 6:5); and the day comes for it — *all the proud, yea, and all that do wickedly, shall be stubble* (Malachi 4:1). The sun shines on the lawless, but the day that burns as an oven is appointed.$n$,$n$*Because it beholds the lawlessness and unrighteousness of men, namely fornications, adulteries, thefts, extortions, idolatries, drunkenness, murders, strife, jealousies, evil-speakings, murmurings, whisperings, divinations, and such like, which are not well-pleasing to Elohim.* It ain't new. The catalog of sins under which the very light is grieved is the indictment of every age. From the flood-world on, *GOD saw that the wickedness of man was great in the earth, and that every imagination of the thoughts of his heart was only evil continually* (Genesis 6:5); and the day comes for it — *all the proud, yea, and all that do wickedly, shall be stubble* (Malachi 4:1). The sun shines on the lawless, but the day that burns as an oven is appointed.$n$),
(13377,$n$On the sixth day the Lord forms man — and though 2 Enoch tells it as a making from *seven consistencies: one, his flesh from the earth... seven, his soul from my breath* (2 Enoch 30:10), the kernel is Moses' own account: man is of the dust and of the breath of Elohim, and is set as His regent. The Lord names him *a second angel, honourable, great and glorious, and I appointed him as ruler to rule on earth* (2 Enoch 30:12). Genesis says it plainly: *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) formed man of the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life; and man became a living soul* (Genesis 2:7); *Let us make man in our image, after our likeness: and let them have dominion* (Genesis 1:26). The psalmist marvels at this same crowning: *What is man, that thou art mindful of him? and the son of Adam, that thou visitest him?... thou hast crowned him with glory and honour. Thou madest him to have dominion over the works of thy hands* (Psalms 8:4-6). It ain't new — strip the seven parts and the four-star etymology, and what remains is the dust-formed, breath-quickened, image-bearing man Genesis sets to rule.$n$,$n$On the sixth day the Lord forms man — and though 2 Enoch tells it as a making from *seven consistencies: one, his flesh from the earth... seven, his soul from my breath* (2 Enoch 30:10), the kernel is Moses' own account: man is of the dust and of the breath of Elohim, and is set as His regent. The Lord names him *a second angel, honourable, great and glorious, and I appointed him as ruler to rule on earth* (2 Enoch 30:12). Genesis says it plainly: *And Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) formed man of the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life; and man became a living soul* (Genesis 2:7); *Let us make man in our image, after our likeness: and let them have dominion* (Genesis 1:26). The psalmist marvels at this same crowning: *What is man, that thou art mindful of him? and the son of Adam, that thou visitest him? For thou hast made him a little lower than the angels, and hast crowned him with glory and honour. Thou madest him to have dominion over the works of thy hands; thou hast put all things under his feet:* (Psalm 8:4–6). It ain't new — strip the seven parts and the four-star etymology, and what remains is the dust-formed, breath-quickened, image-bearing man Genesis sets to rule.$n$),
(13384,$n$Here is the keystone the Lord lays for Enoch: *I appointed the eighth day also, that the eighth day should be the first-created after my work, and that the first seven revolve in the form of the seventh thousand, and that at the beginning of the eighth thousand there should be a time of not-counting, endless, with neither years nor months nor weeks nor days nor hours* (2 Enoch 33:1). The reckoning of a day as a thousand years is the apostle's own measure: *be not ignorant of this one thing, that one day is with the Lord as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day* (2 Peter 3:8) — for to Him *a thousand years in thy sight are but as yesterday when it is past* (Psalms 90:4). And the seventh-day rest opens onto a rest still remaining: *There remaineth therefore a rest to the people of Elohim (God)* (Hebrews 4:9), when the old order passes: *And I saw a new heaven and a new earth: for the first heaven and the first earth were passed away* (Revelation 21:1). It ain't new — the eighth day beyond the seven thousand is the everlasting sabbath-rest the Torah's seventh day always pointed toward, measured by the Lord's own thousand-year day.$n$,$n$Here is the keystone the Lord lays for Enoch: *I appointed the eighth day also, that the eighth day should be the first-created after my work, and that the first seven revolve in the form of the seventh thousand, and that at the beginning of the eighth thousand there should be a time of not-counting, endless, with neither years nor months nor weeks nor days nor hours* (2 Enoch 33:1). The reckoning of a day as a thousand years is the apostle's own measure: *be not ignorant of this one thing, that one day is with Yahuah (Lord) as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day* (2 Peter 3:8) — for to Him *a thousand years in thy sight are but as yesterday when it is past* (Psalms 90:4). And the seventh-day rest opens onto a rest still remaining: *There remaineth therefore a rest to the people of Elohim (God)* (Hebrews 4:9), when the old order passes: *And I saw a new heaven and a new earth: for the first heaven and the first earth were passed away* (Revelation 21:1). It ain't new — the eighth day beyond the seven thousand is the everlasting sabbath-rest the Torah's seventh day always pointed toward, measured by the Lord's own thousand-year day.$n$),
(14085,$n$Baruch warns prospering Babylon not to be boastful, *For assuredly in its own season shall the (divine) wrath awake against thee, Which now in long-suffering is held in as it were by reins.* This is no new threat: the Prophet sees an appointed time — *the vision is yet for an appointed time... though it tarry, wait for it* (Hab 2:3) — and Moses warns that recompense waits in due time — *their foot shall slide in due time: for the day of their calamity is at hand* (Deut 32:35). The apostle names the reins as mercy: *the Lord is not slack... but is longsuffering* (2 Pet 3:9). It ain't new — that judgment is held back in long-suffering and breaks in its appointed season is Moses, the Prophets, and the apostles together.$n$,$n$Baruch warns prospering Babylon not to be boastful, *For assuredly in its own season shall the (divine) wrath awake against thee, Which now in long-suffering is held in as it were by reins.* This is no new threat: the Prophet sees an appointed time — *the vision is yet for an appointed time... though it tarry, wait for it* (Hab 2:3) — and Moses warns that recompense waits in due time — *their foot shall slide in due time: for the day of their calamity is at hand* (Deut 32:35). The apostle names the reins as mercy: *Yahuah (Lord) is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness; but is longsuffering to us-ward* (2 Peter 3:9). It ain't new — that judgment is held back in long-suffering and breaks in its appointed season is Moses, the Prophets, and the apostles together.$n$),
(14089,$n$The charge against the nations: *ye are guilty Because ye have always trodden down the earth, And used the creation unrighteously. For I have always benefited you. And ye have always been ungrateful for the beneficence.* This is the apostle's indictment of the nations — given so much good, they returned no thanks: *when they knew Elohim, they glorified him not as Elohim, neither were thankful* (Rom 1:21) — and Moses' warning against forgetting the Giver: *thou forget Yahuah Elohaycha* (Deut 8:11). It ain't new — that the nations are guilty for abusing a creation freely given and giving no thanks is the apostle's word and Moses' caution.$n$,$n$The charge against the nations: *ye are guilty Because ye have always trodden down the earth, And used the creation unrighteously. For I have always benefited you. And ye have always been ungrateful for the beneficence.* This is the apostle's indictment of the nations — given so much good, they returned no thanks: *when they knew Elohim, they glorified him not as Elohim, neither were thankful* (Rom 1:21) — and Moses' warning against forgetting the Giver: *Beware that thou forget not Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God)* (Deuteronomy 8:11). It ain't new — that the nations are guilty for abusing a creation freely given and giving no thanks is the apostle's word and Moses' caution.$n$),
(14094,$n$The LORD answers Baruch's whole complaint with the law: *Man would not rightly have understood My judgement, unless he had accepted the law, and I had instructed him in understanding. But now, because he transgressed wittingly... he shall be tormented.* This is the Torah's own claim — that the law gives wisdom and is itself life and understanding — *The law of Yahuah is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah is sure, making wise the simple* (Ps 19:7); *for it is your wisdom and your understanding in the sight of the nations* (Deut 4:6). The law is *holy, and just, and good* (Rom 7:12), and judges the man who sins against it knowingly. It ain't new — that Yahuah's judgment is understood only through His law, which abides as Israel's light, is the testimony of Moses, the Psalms, and the apostle.$n$,$n$The LORD answers Baruch's whole complaint with the law: *Man would not rightly have understood My judgement, unless he had accepted the law, and I had instructed him in understanding. But now, because he transgressed wittingly... he shall be tormented.* This is the Torah's own claim — that the law gives wisdom and is itself life and understanding — *The law of Yahuah is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of Yahuah is sure, making wise the simple* (Ps 19:7); *for this is your wisdom and your understanding in the sight of the nations* (Deuteronomy 4:6). The law is *holy, and just, and good* (Rom 7:12), and judges the man who sins against it knowingly. It ain't new — that Yahuah's judgment is understood only through His law, which abides as Israel's light, is the testimony of Moses, the Psalms, and the apostle.$n$),
(14114,$n$Baruch asks the question every sufferer asks of the appointed woes: *Will that tribulation which is to be continue a long time, and will that necessity embrace many years?* (2 Baruch 26:1). It is the cry of the souls under the altar — *How long, O Lord, holy and true, dost thou not judge and avenge our blood?* (Revelation 6:10) — and the answer the Messiah gives is that the days are measured and cut short, *except those days should be shortened, there should no flesh be saved: but for the elect's sake those days shall be shortened* (Matthew 24:22). It ain't new — the saints have always asked how long, and the days are numbered.$n$,$n$Baruch asks the question every sufferer asks of the appointed woes: *Will that tribulation which is to be continue a long time, and will that necessity embrace many years?* (2 Baruch 26:1). It is the cry of the souls under the altar — *How long, O Yahuah (Lord), holy and true, dost thou not judge and avenge our blood on them that dwell on the earth?* (Revelation 6:10) — and the answer the Messiah gives is that the days are measured and cut short, *except those days should be shortened, there should no flesh be saved: but for the elect's sake those days shall be shortened* (Matthew 24:22). It ain't new — the saints have always asked how long, and the days are numbered.$n$),
(14120,$n$When the appointed measure is filled, *the Messiah shall then begin to be revealed* (2 Baruch 29:3). This is the Anointed of David's hope, made manifest in his season — the One whom the Father sets forth, *I have set my king upon my holy hill of Zion* (Psalms 2:6), the rod out of the stem of Jesse, *with righteousness shall he judge the poor... and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked* (Isaiah 11:4). His unveiling is the appearing the apostles waited for, *who shall be revealed in his time* (1 Timothy 6:14-15). It ain't new — the Messiah revealed in the end is the King the Psalm and Isaiah already crowned.$n$,$n$When the appointed measure is filled, *the Messiah shall then begin to be revealed* (2 Baruch 29:3). This is the Anointed of David's hope, made manifest in his season — the One whom the Father sets forth, *Yet have I set my king upon my holy hill of Zion* (Psalms 2:6), the rod out of the stem of Jesse, *with righteousness shall he judge the poor... and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked* (Isaiah 11:4). His unveiling is the appearing the apostles waited for, *the appearing of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ): Which in his times he shall shew, who is the blessed and only Potentate, the King of kings, and Lord of lords;* (1 Timothy 6:14–15). It ain't new — the Messiah revealed in the end is the King the Psalm and Isaiah already crowned.$n$),
(14178,$n$The third rain is black: *the mingling of all sins, which the nations afterwards wrought after the death of those righteous men, and the wickedness of the land of Egypt, wherein they did wickedly in the service wherewith they made their sons to serve.* The cruelty of Egypt's bondage is the darkness here named. It ain't new — *the Egyptians made the children of Yashar'el to serve with rigour... and made their lives bitter with hard bondage* (Exod 1:13-14), and *Pharaoh charged all his people... Every son that is born ye shall cast into the river* (Exod 1:22); yet *these also perished at last*, as Yahuah remembered his own.$n$,$n$The third rain is black: *the mingling of all sins, which the nations afterwards wrought after the death of those righteous men, and the wickedness of the land of Egypt, wherein they did wickedly in the service wherewith they made their sons to serve.* The cruelty of Egypt's bondage is the darkness here named. It ain't new — *the Egyptians made the children of Yashar'el (Israel) to serve with rigour: And they made their lives bitter with hard bondage* (Exodus 1:13–14), and *Pharaoh charged all his people... Every son that is born ye shall cast into the river* (Exod 1:22); yet *these also perished at last*, as Yahuah remembered his own.$n$),
(14181,$n$The fifth rain is black: *the works which the Amorites wrought, and the spells of their incantations... and the wickedness of their mysteries, and the mingling of their pollution. But even Yashar'el was then polluted by sins in the days of the judges, though they saw many signs.* The land's idolatry drew Israel after it. It ain't new — Moses warned the nations were driven out *for the wickedness of these nations* (Deut 9:4-5), yet in Judges *the children of Yashar'el did evil in the sight of Yahuah, and served Baalim... and forsook Yahuah Elohim of their fathers* (Judg 2:11-12) — the very pollution Ramael names.$n$,$n$The fifth rain is black: *the works which the Amorites wrought, and the spells of their incantations... and the wickedness of their mysteries, and the mingling of their pollution. But even Yashar'el was then polluted by sins in the days of the judges, though they saw many signs.* The land's idolatry drew Israel after it. It ain't new — Moses warned the nations were driven out *for the wickedness of these nations* (Deut 9:4-5), yet in Judges *the children of Yashar'el (Israel) did evil in the sight of Yahuah (LORD), and served Baalim: And they forsook Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) of their fathers* (Judges 2:11–12) — the very pollution Ramael names.$n$);
